WEBVTT

1
00:01:24.202 --> 00:01:25.787
I feel like you're driving me
to a court-martial.

2
00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.914
This is crazy. What did I do?

3
00:01:27.997 --> 00:01:29.457
I feel like you're going to pull over
and snuff me.

4
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.959
What. you're not allowed to talk?
Hey. Forrest!

5
00:01:32.043 --> 00:01:33.252
We can talk. sir.

6
00:01:33.336 --> 00:01:37.131
- Oh. I see. So it's personal?
- No. you intimidate them.

7
00:01:37.215 --> 00:01:40.384
Good God. you're a woman.
I honestly... I couldn't have called that.

8
00:01:40.468 --> 00:01:42.929
I mean. I'd apologize.
but isn't that what we're going for here?

9
00:01:43.012 --> 00:01:45.807
- I thought of you as a soldier first.
- I'm an airman.

10
00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.642
You have. actually.
excellent bone structure. there.

11
00:01:47.725 --> 00:01:50.478
I'm kind of having a hard time
not looking at you now.

12
00:01:50.561 --> 00:01:53.397
Is that weird? Come on. it's okay. laugh.

13
00:01:53.773 --> 00:01:56.275
- Sir. I have a question to ask.
- Yes. please.

14
00:01:56.359 --> 00:02:00.029
Is it true you went 12 for 12
with last year's Maxim cover models?

15
00:02:00.112 --> 00:02:02.281
That is an excellent question.
Yes and no.

16
00:02:02.365 --> 00:02:03.825
March and I had a scheduling conflict.

17
00:02:03.908 --> 00:02:06.828
but fortunately.
the Christmas cover was twins.

18
00:02:06.911 --> 00:02:09.789
Anything else? You're kidding me
with the hand up. right?

19
00:02:09.872 --> 00:02:13.751
- Is it cool if I take a picture with you?
- Yes. It's very cool.

20
00:02:17.338 --> 00:02:18.673
All right.

21
00:02:18.756 --> 00:02:20.842
I don't want to see this
on your MySpace page.

22
00:02:20.925 --> 00:02:22.510
Please. no gang signs.

23
00:02:22.593 --> 00:02:24.178
No. throw it up. I'm kidding.

24
00:02:24.262 --> 00:02:27.265
Yeah. peace. I love peace.
I'd be out of a job with peace.

25
00:02:27.431 --> 00:02:31.435
Come on. Hurry up. Just click it.
Don't change any settings. Just click it.

26
00:02:37.024 --> 00:02:39.068
- What's going on?
- Contact left!

27
00:02:39.151 --> 00:02:40.862
What have we got?

28
00:02:42.113 --> 00:02:44.198
Jimmy. stay with Stark!

29
00:02:44.282 --> 00:02:45.324
- Stay down!
- Yeah.

30
00:02:51.664 --> 00:02:53.207
Son of a bitch!

31
00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.670
- Wait. wait. wait! Give me a gun!
- Stay here!

32
00:03:26.908 --> 00:03:28.284
Whoa!

33
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.043
Tony Stark.

34
00:04:20.544 --> 00:04:22.964
Visionary. Genius.

35
00:04:23.798 --> 00:04:25.675
American patriot.

36
00:04:25.758 --> 00:04:26.926
Even from an early age.

37
00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:29.470
the son of legendary
weapons developer Howard Stark

38
00:04:29.553 --> 00:04:33.099
quickly stole the spotlight
with his brilliant and unique mind.

39
00:04:33.182 --> 00:04:36.644
At age four.
he built his first circuit board.

40
00:04:36.727 --> 00:04:38.896
At age six. his first engine.

41
00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.401
And at 17. he graduated
summa cum laude from MIT.

42
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.737
Then. the passing of a titan.

43
00:04:48.364 --> 00:04:51.242
Howard Stark's lifelong friend
and ally. Obadiah Stane.

44
00:04:51.325 --> 00:04:54.745
steps in to help fill the gap
left by the legendary founder.

45
00:04:54.954 --> 00:04:58.290
until. at age 21. the prodigal son returns

46
00:04:58.374 --> 00:05:01.752
and is anointed the new CEO
of Stark industries.

47
00:05:01.836 --> 00:05:03.170
With the keys to the kingdom.

48
00:05:03.254 --> 00:05:06.048
Tony ushers in a new era
for his father's legacy.

49
00:05:06.132 --> 00:05:10.177
creating smarter weapons.
advanced robotics. satellite targeting.

50
00:05:10.261 --> 00:05:14.140
Today. Tony Stark has changed
the face of the weapons industry

51
00:05:14.223 --> 00:05:17.018
by ensuring freedom
and protecting America

52
00:05:17.101 --> 00:05:19.687
and her interests around the globe.

53
00:05:28.029 --> 00:05:30.364
As liaison to Stark Industries.

54
00:05:30.948 --> 00:05:34.702
I've had the unique privilege
of serving with a real patriot.

55
00:05:34.869 --> 00:05:38.539
He is my friend
and he is my great mentor.

56
00:05:38.998 --> 00:05:41.208
Ladies and gentlemen. it is my honor

57
00:05:41.292 --> 00:05:45.629
to present this year's Apogee Award
to Mr. Tony Stark.

58
00:05:52.845 --> 00:05:54.138
Tony?

59
00:06:06.442 --> 00:06:09.028
- Thank you. Colonel.
- Thanks for the save.

60
00:06:09.111 --> 00:06:12.782
This is beautiful. Thank you.
Thank you all very much.

61
00:06:12.865 --> 00:06:14.325
This is wonderful.

62
00:06:16.202 --> 00:06:18.204
Well. I'm not Tony Stark.

63
00:06:20.081 --> 00:06:25.211
But if I were Tony.
I would tell you how honored I feel

64
00:06:25.544 --> 00:06:30.299
and what a joy it is
to receive this very prestigious award.

65
00:06:30.716 --> 00:06:32.134
Tony. you know...

66
00:06:32.218 --> 00:06:36.138
The best thing about Tony
is also the worst thing.

67
00:06:36.222 --> 00:06:37.640
He's always working.

68
00:06:39.725 --> 00:06:43.145
Work it! Come on!

69
00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:50.236
- We should just stay till the morning.
- You are unbelievable.

70
00:06:50.319 --> 00:06:53.614
- Oh. no! Did they rope you into this?
- Nobody roped me into anything!

71
00:06:53.697 --> 00:06:54.657
- I'm so sorry.
- But they told me that

72
00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.618
if I presented you with an award.
you'd be deeply honored.

73
00:06:57.701 --> 00:06:59.620
Of course I'd be deeply honored.
And it's you. that's great.

74
00:06:59.703 --> 00:07:01.413
- So when do we do it?
- It's right here.

75
00:07:01.497 --> 00:07:03.624
- Here you go.
- There it is. That was easy.

76
00:07:03.707 --> 00:07:05.084
- I'm so sorry.
- Yeah. it's okay.

77
00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:07.461
Wow! Would you look at that?
That's something else.

78
00:07:07.545 --> 00:07:09.130
I don't have any of those
floating around.

79
00:07:09.213 --> 00:07:11.340
We're gonna let it ride!

80
00:07:12.424 --> 00:07:14.552
Give me a hand. will you?
Give me a little something-something.

81
00:07:14.635 --> 00:07:15.761
Okay. you. too.

82
00:07:15.845 --> 00:07:17.721
- I don't blow on a man's dice.
- Come on. honey bear.

83
00:07:17.805 --> 00:07:20.307
There it is.
Lieutenant Colonel Rhodes rolls! And...

84
00:07:20.391 --> 00:07:21.642
Two craps. Line away.

85
00:07:21.725 --> 00:07:23.561
- That's what happens.
- Worse things have happened.

86
00:07:23.644 --> 00:07:25.062
I think we're gonna be fine.
Color me up. will you?

87
00:07:25.604 --> 00:07:26.647
- This is where I exit.
- All right.

88
00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:27.690
Tomorrow. don't be late.

89
00:07:27.773 --> 00:07:29.024
- Yeah. you can count on it.
- I'm serious!

90
00:07:29.108 --> 00:07:30.401
I know. I know.

91
00:07:30.484 --> 00:07:34.029
Render unto Caesar
that which is Caesar's. There you go.

92
00:07:38.409 --> 00:07:40.703
Mr. Stark! Excuse me. Mr. Stark!

93
00:07:41.036 --> 00:07:43.289
Christine Everhart.
Vanity Fair magazine.

94
00:07:43.372 --> 00:07:44.456
Can I ask you a couple of questions?

95
00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.041
- She's cute.
- She's all right?

96
00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:47.168
- Hi.
- Hi.

97
00:07:47.251 --> 00:07:49.170
- Yeah. Okay. go.
- It's okay?

98
00:07:49.253 --> 00:07:51.088
You've been called
the da Vinci of our time.

99
00:07:51.172 --> 00:07:54.008
- What do you say to that?
- Absolutely ridiculous. I don't paint.

100
00:07:54.091 --> 00:07:55.676
And what do you say
to your other nickname?

101
00:07:55.759 --> 00:07:56.969
"The Merchant of Death"?

102
00:07:57.052 --> 00:07:58.596
That's not bad.

103
00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:02.474
- Let me guess. Berkeley?
- Brown. actually.

104
00:08:02.725 --> 00:08:05.102
Well. Ms. Brown.

105
00:08:05.686 --> 00:08:07.646
it's an imperfect world.
but it's the only one we've got.

106
00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:10.441
I guarantee you. the day weapons are
no longer needed to keep the peace.

107
00:08:10.524 --> 00:08:12.693
I'll start making bricks and beams
for baby hospitals.

108
00:08:12.776 --> 00:08:13.861
Rehearse that much?

109
00:08:13.944 --> 00:08:15.613
Every night in front of the mirror
before bedtime.

110
00:08:15.696 --> 00:08:18.032
- I can see that.
- I'd like to show you first-hand.

111
00:08:18.115 --> 00:08:20.367
All I want is a serious answer.

112
00:08:20.451 --> 00:08:22.703
Okay. here's serious.
My old man had a philosophy.

113
00:08:22.786 --> 00:08:25.206
"Peace means having a bigger stick
than the other guy."

114
00:08:25.289 --> 00:08:27.541
That's a great line
coming from the guy selling the sticks.

115
00:08:27.625 --> 00:08:30.419
My father helped defeat the Nazis.
He worked on the Manhattan Project.

116
00:08:30.502 --> 00:08:33.088
A lot of people.
including your professors at Brown.

117
00:08:33.172 --> 00:08:34.381
would call that being a hero.

118
00:08:34.465 --> 00:08:36.634
And a lot of people
would also call that war profiteering.

119
00:08:36.717 --> 00:08:38.886
Tell me. do you plan to report
on the millions we've saved

120
00:08:38.969 --> 00:08:40.721
by advancing medical technology

121
00:08:40.804 --> 00:08:43.140
or kept from starvation
with our intelli-crops?

122
00:08:43.224 --> 00:08:46.477
All those breakthroughs.
military funding. honey.

123
00:08:48.103 --> 00:08:49.980
You ever lose an hour of sleep
your whole life?

124
00:08:50.064 --> 00:08:51.982
I'd be prepared to lose a few with you.

125
00:09:06.163 --> 00:09:07.831
Good morning. It's 7:00 a.m.

126
00:09:07.915 --> 00:09:11.585
The weather in Malibu
is 72 degrees with scattered clouds.

127
00:09:11.794 --> 00:09:15.089
The surf conditions are fair
with waist-to-shoulder high lines.

128
00:09:15.172 --> 00:09:17.633
High tide will be at 10:52 a.m.

129
00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:35.943
Tony?

130
00:09:37.361 --> 00:09:38.696
Hey. Tony?

131
00:10:00.467 --> 00:10:02.761
You are not authorized
to access this area.

132
00:10:02.886 --> 00:10:05.597
- Jesus.
- That's Jarvis. He runs the house.

133
00:10:06.098 --> 00:10:08.726
I've got your clothes here.
They've been dry-cleaned and pressed.

134
00:10:08.809 --> 00:10:10.561
and there's a car waiting for you outside

135
00:10:10.644 --> 00:10:12.938
that will take you anywhere
you'd like to go.

136
00:10:13.272 --> 00:10:16.775
- You must be the famous Pepper Potts.
- Indeed I am.

137
00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.281
After all these years. Tony still has you
picking up the dry-cleaning.

138
00:10:22.364 --> 00:10:25.701
I do anything and everything
that Mr. Stark requires.

139
00:10:25.784 --> 00:10:28.579
including. occasionally.
taking out the trash.

140
00:10:28.662 --> 00:10:29.747
Will that be all?

141
00:10:46.722 --> 00:10:48.307
Give me an exploded view.

142
00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:51.643
The compression in cylinder three
appears to be low.

143
00:10:52.019 --> 00:10:53.270
Log that.

144
00:10:57.024 --> 00:10:59.109
- I'm gonna try again. right now.
- Please don't turn down my music.

145
00:10:59.193 --> 00:11:00.194
I'll keep you posted.

146
00:11:00.277 --> 00:11:02.029
You are supposed to be
halfway around the world right now.

147
00:11:02.112 --> 00:11:04.490
- How'd she take it?
- Like a champ.

148
00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.116
Why are you trying to hustle me
out of here?

149
00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.910
Your flight was scheduled to leave
an hour and a half ago.

150
00:11:07.993 --> 00:11:10.120
That's funny. I thought with it being
my plane and all.

151
00:11:10.204 --> 00:11:11.747
that it would just wait for me
to get there.

152
00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.582
Tony. I need to speak to you
about a couple things

153
00:11:13.665 --> 00:11:14.750
before I get you out of the door.

154
00:11:14.833 --> 00:11:17.086
Doesn't it kind of defeat the whole
purpose of having your own plane

155
00:11:17.169 --> 00:11:18.379
if it departs before you arrive?

156
00:11:18.462 --> 00:11:21.840
Larry called. He's got another buyer
for the Jackson Pollock in the wings.

157
00:11:21.924 --> 00:11:23.550
Do you want it? Yes or no.

158
00:11:23.634 --> 00:11:25.719
Is it a good representation
of his spring period?

159
00:11:26.512 --> 00:11:29.014
No. The Springs was actually
the neighborhood in East Hampton

160
00:11:29.098 --> 00:11:30.349
where he lived and worked.

161
00:11:30.432 --> 00:11:31.934
- not "spring" like the season.
- So?

162
00:11:32.017 --> 00:11:36.397
I think it's a fair example.
I think it's incredibly overpriced.

163
00:11:37.272 --> 00:11:39.858
I need it. Buy it. Store it.

164
00:11:40.609 --> 00:11:43.195
Okay.
The MIT commencement speech...

165
00:11:43.278 --> 00:11:46.073
ls in June. Please. don't harangue me
about stuff that's way. way. down...

166
00:11:46.156 --> 00:11:48.575
They're haranguing me.
so I'm gonna say yes.

167
00:11:48.659 --> 00:11:50.160
Deflect it and absorb it.
Don't transmit it back to me.

168
00:11:50.244 --> 00:11:51.578
I need you to sign this
before you get on the plane.

169
00:11:51.662 --> 00:11:53.580
What are you trying to get rid of me for?
What. you got plans?

170
00:11:53.664 --> 00:11:56.208
- As a matter of fact. I do.
- I don't like it when you have plans.

171
00:11:56.291 --> 00:11:58.335
I'm allowed to have plans
on my birthday.

172
00:11:58.419 --> 00:11:59.920
- It's your birthday?
- Yes.

173
00:12:00.003 --> 00:12:01.463
I knew that. Already?

174
00:12:01.547 --> 00:12:05.134
Yeah. isn't that strange?
It's the same day as last year.

175
00:12:06.009 --> 00:12:08.595
- Get yourself something nice from me.
- I already did.

176
00:12:08.679 --> 00:12:11.140
- And?
- It was very nice.

177
00:12:11.223 --> 00:12:14.685
- Yeah.
- Very tasteful. Thank you. Mr. Stark.

178
00:12:15.352 --> 00:12:17.479
You're welcome. Miss Potts.

179
00:12:20.649 --> 00:12:21.650
Okay.

180
00:12:40.043 --> 00:12:43.630
You're good.
I thought I lost you back there.

181
00:12:44.256 --> 00:12:48.218
You did. sir.
I had to cut across Mulholland.

182
00:12:48.552 --> 00:12:49.845
I got you. I got you.

183
00:12:49.928 --> 00:12:51.346
What's wrong with you?

184
00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.973
- What?
- Three hours.

185
00:12:53.056 --> 00:12:55.184
I got caught doing a piece
for Vanity Fair.

186
00:12:55.267 --> 00:12:57.269
For three hours. For three hours
you got me standing here.

187
00:12:57.352 --> 00:12:59.897
Waiting on you now. Let's go. Come on.

188
00:13:00.522 --> 00:13:02.524
Wheels up! Rock and roll!

189
00:13:10.574 --> 00:13:13.160
- What you reading. platypus?
- Nothing.

190
00:13:13.243 --> 00:13:15.454
Come on. sour patch. Don't be mad.

191
00:13:15.537 --> 00:13:18.248
I told you. I'm not mad.
I'm indifferent. okay?

192
00:13:18.332 --> 00:13:19.791
- I said I was sorry.
- Good morning. Mr. Stark.

193
00:13:19.875 --> 00:13:21.001
You don't need to apologize to me.
I'm your man.

194
00:13:21.084 --> 00:13:22.127
Hi. I told him I was sorry. but he...

195
00:13:22.211 --> 00:13:23.587
- I'm just indifferent right now.
- Hot towel?

196
00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.880
You don't respect yourself.

197
00:13:24.963 --> 00:13:26.340
- so I know you don't respect me.
- I respect you.

198
00:13:26.423 --> 00:13:27.758
I'm just your babysitter.

199
00:13:27.841 --> 00:13:30.344
So. when you need
your diaper changed... Thank you.

200
00:13:30.427 --> 00:13:32.638
Let me know
and I'll get you a bottle. okay?

201
00:13:32.721 --> 00:13:34.348
Hey! Heat up the sake. will you?

202
00:13:34.431 --> 00:13:35.849
- Thanks for reminding me.
- No. I'm not talking...

203
00:13:35.933 --> 00:13:37.684
We're not drinking.
We're working right now.

204
00:13:37.768 --> 00:13:40.187
- You can't have sashimi without sake.
- You are constitutionally

205
00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:41.855
incapable of being responsible.

206
00:13:41.939 --> 00:13:44.483
It would be irresponsible not to drink.
I'm just talking about a nightcap.

207
00:13:44.566 --> 00:13:45.609
Hot sake?

208
00:13:45.692 --> 00:13:49.029
- Yes. two. please.
- No. I'm not drinking. I don't want any.

209
00:13:49.112 --> 00:13:50.447
That's what I'm talking about.

210
00:13:50.531 --> 00:13:53.575
When I get up in the morning
and I'm putting on my uniform.

211
00:13:53.659 --> 00:13:55.452
you know what I recognize?

212
00:13:55.536 --> 00:14:00.749
I see in that mirror that every person
that's got this uniform on got my back!

213
00:14:00.832 --> 00:14:03.544
Hey. you know what?
I'm not like you. I'm not cut out...

214
00:14:03.627 --> 00:14:06.713
No. no. You don't have to be like me!
But you're more than what you are.

215
00:14:06.797 --> 00:14:08.632
Can you excuse me if
I'm a bit distracted here?

216
00:14:08.715 --> 00:14:11.802
No! You can't be distracted right now!
Listen to me!

217
00:14:28.485 --> 00:14:29.444
General.

218
00:14:29.528 --> 00:14:33.115
Welcome. Mr. Stark. We look forward
to your weapons presentation.

219
00:14:33.198 --> 00:14:34.199
Thanks.

220
00:14:36.118 --> 00:14:38.996
Is it better to be feared or respected?

221
00:14:39.162 --> 00:14:42.249
I say. is it too much to ask for both?

222
00:14:43.166 --> 00:14:46.086
With that in mind.
I humbly present the crown jewel

223
00:14:46.169 --> 00:14:47.963
of Stark industries' Freedom Line.

224
00:14:48.046 --> 00:14:49.089
It's the first missile system

225
00:14:49.172 --> 00:14:52.050
to incorporate our proprietary
repulsor technology.

226
00:14:52.134 --> 00:14:56.096
They say the best weapon
is one you never have to fire.

227
00:14:56.179 --> 00:14:58.140
I respectfully disagree.

228
00:14:58.223 --> 00:15:02.269
I prefer the weapon
you only have to fire once.

229
00:15:02.519 --> 00:15:05.731
That's how Dad did it.
That's how America does it.

230
00:15:06.523 --> 00:15:08.650
And it's worked out pretty well so far.

231
00:15:08.734 --> 00:15:10.068
Find an excuse

232
00:15:10.152 --> 00:15:13.447
to let one of these off the chain.
and I personally guarantee you

233
00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:17.075
the bad guys won't even want
to come out of their caves.

234
00:15:35.552 --> 00:15:39.348
For your consideration. the Jericho.

235
00:15:50.942 --> 00:15:51.943
I'll be throwing one of these in

236
00:15:52.027 --> 00:15:54.029
with every purchase
of 500 million or more.

237
00:15:54.112 --> 00:15:55.155
To peace!

238
00:15:56.907 --> 00:15:58.950
- Tony.
- Obie. what are you doing up?

239
00:15:59.034 --> 00:16:01.495
I couldn't sleep till I found out
how it went. How'd it go?

240
00:16:01.578 --> 00:16:03.413
It went great. Looks like it's gonna be
an early Christmas.

241
00:16:03.497 --> 00:16:07.376
Hey! Way to go. my boy!
I'll see you tomorrow. yeah?

242
00:16:07.459 --> 00:16:08.919
Why aren't you wearing those pajamas
I got you?

243
00:16:09.002 --> 00:16:10.587
Good night. Tony.

244
00:16:12.005 --> 00:16:14.466
- Hey. Tony.
- I'm sorry. this is the "fun-vee."

245
00:16:14.549 --> 00:16:16.510
The "hum-drum-vee" is back there.

246
00:16:16.593 --> 00:16:19.304
- Nice job.
- See you back at base.

247
00:17:26.288 --> 00:17:28.457
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

248
00:18:05.035 --> 00:18:06.828
What the hell did you do to me?

249
00:18:07.662 --> 00:18:09.206
What I did?

250
00:18:10.457 --> 00:18:12.250
What I did is to save your life.

251
00:18:12.501 --> 00:18:16.129
I removed all the shrapnel I could.
but there's a lot left.

252
00:18:16.213 --> 00:18:18.048
and it's headed into your atrial septum.

253
00:18:18.757 --> 00:18:20.550
Here. want to see?

254
00:18:21.218 --> 00:18:24.054
I have a souvenir. Take a look.

255
00:18:26.723 --> 00:18:28.934
I've seen many wounds like that
in my village.

256
00:18:29.017 --> 00:18:31.436
We call them the walking dead

257
00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.689
because it takes about a week
for the barbs to reach the vital organs.

258
00:18:34.773 --> 00:18:37.567
- What is this?
- That is an electromagnet.

259
00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:40.487
hooked up to a car battery.

260
00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:43.490
and it's keeping the shrapnel
from entering your heart.

261
00:18:51.748 --> 00:18:53.834
That's right. Smile.

262
00:18:55.544 --> 00:18:59.673
We met once. you know.
at a technical conference in Bern.

263
00:19:00.215 --> 00:19:02.759
- I don't remember.
- No. you wouldn't.

264
00:19:03.093 --> 00:19:06.179
If I had been that drunk.
I wouldn't have been able to stand.

265
00:19:06.263 --> 00:19:09.432
much less give a lecture
on integrated circuits.

266
00:19:09.516 --> 00:19:10.851
Where are we?

267
00:19:12.769 --> 00:19:14.688
Come on. stand up. Stand up!

268
00:19:15.647 --> 00:19:17.691
Just do as I do.

269
00:19:18.358 --> 00:19:20.443
Come on. put your hands up.

270
00:19:22.195 --> 00:19:23.655
Those are my guns.
How did they get my guns?

271
00:19:23.738 --> 00:19:26.116
Do you understand me? Do as I do.

272
00:19:46.595 --> 00:19:50.807
He says. "Welcome. Tony Stark.
the most famous mass murderer"

273
00:19:50.891 --> 00:19:52.726
"in the history of America."

274
00:19:56.146 --> 00:19:57.689
He is honored.

275
00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:01.985
He wants you to build the missile.

276
00:20:03.361 --> 00:20:05.697
The Jericho missile
that you demonstrated.

277
00:20:09.284 --> 00:20:10.452
This one.

278
00:20:15.498 --> 00:20:16.499
I refuse.

279
00:20:27.302 --> 00:20:28.303
Tony!

280
00:21:18.311 --> 00:21:20.647
He wants to know what you think.

281
00:21:21.606 --> 00:21:23.400
I think you got a lot of my weapons.

282
00:21:32.367 --> 00:21:36.496
He says they have everything you need
to build the Jericho missile.

283
00:21:37.122 --> 00:21:39.249
He wants you to make
the list of materials.

284
00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:45.088
He says for you
to start working immediately.

285
00:21:45.171 --> 00:21:48.425
and when you're done.
he will set you free.

286
00:21:51.928 --> 00:21:54.472
- No. he won't.
- No. he won't.

287
00:22:08.069 --> 00:22:10.655
I'm sure they're looking for you. Stark.

288
00:22:10.739 --> 00:22:13.825
But they will never find you
in these mountains.

289
00:22:15.452 --> 00:22:19.205
Look. what you just saw.

290
00:22:19.998 --> 00:22:22.125
that is your legacy. Stark.

291
00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:27.088
Your life's work.
in the hands of those murderers.

292
00:22:27.172 --> 00:22:29.466
Is that how you want to go out?

293
00:22:30.008 --> 00:22:34.971
Is this the last act of defiance
of the great Tony Stark?

294
00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:37.265
Or are you going to
do something about it?

295
00:22:37.348 --> 00:22:42.479
Why should I do anything?
They're going to kill me. you. either way.

296
00:22:42.562 --> 00:22:45.815
And if they don't.
I'll probably be dead in a week.

297
00:22:45.899 --> 00:22:47.275
Well. then.

298
00:22:47.859 --> 00:22:50.987
this is a very important week for you.
isn't it?

299
00:22:53.782 --> 00:22:57.285
If this is going to be my work station.
I want it well-lit. I want these up.

300
00:22:57.535 --> 00:23:00.580
I need welding gear.
I don't care if it's acetylene or propane.

301
00:23:00.663 --> 00:23:02.832
I need a soldering station. I need
helmets. I'm gonna need goggles.

302
00:23:02.916 --> 00:23:05.960
I would like a smelting cup.
I need two sets of precision tools.

303
00:23:19.349 --> 00:23:21.768
- How many languages do you speak?
- A lot.

304
00:23:21.851 --> 00:23:24.562
But apparently.
not enough for this place.

305
00:23:24.646 --> 00:23:26.689
They speak Arabic. Urdu.

306
00:23:26.773 --> 00:23:30.193
Dari. Pashto. Mongolian.
Farsi. Russian.

307
00:23:31.361 --> 00:23:35.657
- Who are these people?
- They are your loyal customers. sir.

308
00:23:36.324 --> 00:23:38.368
They call themselves the Ten Rings.

309
00:23:47.752 --> 00:23:49.212
You know. we might be more productive

310
00:23:49.295 --> 00:23:52.090
if you include me
in the planning process.

311
00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:02.892
Okay. we don't need this.

312
00:24:04.853 --> 00:24:06.312
What is that?

313
00:24:07.814 --> 00:24:10.150
That's palladium. 0.15 grams.

314
00:24:10.775 --> 00:24:14.237
We need at least 1.6. so why don't
you go break down the other 11?

315
00:24:16.906 --> 00:24:18.825
What's he doing?

316
00:24:19.367 --> 00:24:20.743
Working.

317
00:24:30.795 --> 00:24:33.756
Careful.
Careful. we only get one shot at this.

318
00:24:33.840 --> 00:24:36.551
Relax. I have steady hands.

319
00:24:37.510 --> 00:24:40.054
Why do you think you're still alive?

320
00:24:46.311 --> 00:24:49.689
- What do I call you?
- My name is Yinsen.

321
00:24:50.190 --> 00:24:52.609
Yinsen. Nice to meet you.

322
00:24:53.443 --> 00:24:55.320
Nice to meet you. too.

323
00:25:35.360 --> 00:25:37.654
That doesn't look like a Jericho missile.

324
00:25:37.987 --> 00:25:41.199
That's because
it's a miniaturized arc reactor.

325
00:25:41.532 --> 00:25:44.327
I got a big one
powering my factory at home.

326
00:25:44.661 --> 00:25:47.413
It should keep the shrapnel
out of my heart.

327
00:25:47.497 --> 00:25:49.165
But what could it generate?

328
00:25:49.249 --> 00:25:53.836
If my math is right. and it always is.
three gigajoules per second.

329
00:25:54.295 --> 00:25:56.756
That could run your heart
for 50 lifetimes.

330
00:25:56.839 --> 00:25:59.926
Yeah. Or something big for 15 minutes.

331
00:26:08.893 --> 00:26:12.272
- This is our ticket out of here.
- What is it?

332
00:26:13.773 --> 00:26:15.358
Flatten them out and look.

333
00:26:17.902 --> 00:26:18.903
Oh. wow.

334
00:26:21.990 --> 00:26:23.574
Impressive.

335
00:26:49.642 --> 00:26:51.561
Good.

336
00:26:51.644 --> 00:26:54.314
Good roll. Good roll.

337
00:26:55.106 --> 00:26:56.983
You still haven't told me
where you're from.

338
00:26:57.066 --> 00:26:59.902
I'm from a small town called Gulmira.

339
00:27:00.403 --> 00:27:03.406
- It's actually a nice place.
- Got a family?

340
00:27:03.740 --> 00:27:08.119
Yes. and I will see them
when I leave here.

341
00:27:08.911 --> 00:27:10.538
And you. Stark?

342
00:27:14.625 --> 00:27:16.836
- No.
- No?

343
00:27:18.629 --> 00:27:21.215
So you're a man who has everything

344
00:27:21.924 --> 00:27:23.259
and nothing.

345
00:28:08.888 --> 00:28:11.974
It doesn't look anything like the picture.

346
00:28:12.058 --> 00:28:13.643
Maybe it's been modified.

347
00:28:13.726 --> 00:28:14.769
The tail is wrong.

348
00:28:14.852 --> 00:28:15.853
It's just backwards.

349
00:29:01.691 --> 00:29:02.859
Relax.

350
00:29:11.951 --> 00:29:14.162
The bow and arrow

351
00:29:14.245 --> 00:29:17.123
once was the pinnacle
of weapons technology.

352
00:29:19.709 --> 00:29:22.086
It allowed the great Genghis Khan

353
00:29:22.879 --> 00:29:25.882
to rule from the Pacific to the Ukraine.

354
00:29:26.466 --> 00:29:30.219
An empire twice the size
of Alexander the Great

355
00:29:31.345 --> 00:29:34.891
and four times
the size of the Roman Empire.

356
00:29:38.519 --> 00:29:39.854
But today.

357
00:29:40.688 --> 00:29:44.066
whoever holds the latest Stark weapons

358
00:29:45.109 --> 00:29:46.986
rules these lands.

359
00:29:49.322 --> 00:29:50.698
And soon.

360
00:29:53.659 --> 00:29:55.411
it will be my turn.

361
00:30:08.591 --> 00:30:10.092
Why have you failed me?

362
00:30:10.927 --> 00:30:12.595
We're working.

363
00:30:13.095 --> 00:30:14.263
Diligently.

364
00:30:14.514 --> 00:30:16.265
I let you live.

365
00:30:18.601 --> 00:30:20.478
This is how you repay me?

366
00:30:21.145 --> 00:30:23.481
It's very complex.

367
00:30:23.940 --> 00:30:26.234
He's trying very hard.

368
00:30:26.567 --> 00:30:27.610
On his knees.

369
00:30:32.281 --> 00:30:33.950
You think I'm a fool?

370
00:30:34.742 --> 00:30:35.993
I'll get the truth.

371
00:30:36.744 --> 00:30:38.079
We're both working.

372
00:30:45.545 --> 00:30:46.671
Open your mouth.

373
00:30:47.004 --> 00:30:48.047
What does he want?

374
00:30:48.297 --> 00:30:50.424
You think I'm a fool?

375
00:30:54.262 --> 00:30:55.805
What's going on?

376
00:30:56.305 --> 00:30:58.808
Tell me the truth.

377
00:30:58.975 --> 00:31:00.476
He's building your Jericho.

378
00:31:03.521 --> 00:31:05.982
What do you want? A delivery date?

379
00:31:13.239 --> 00:31:14.615
I need him.

380
00:31:16.742 --> 00:31:18.286
Good assistant.

381
00:31:23.082 --> 00:31:27.086
You have till tomorrow
to assemble my missile.

382
00:32:31.859 --> 00:32:34.236
Okay? Can you move?

383
00:32:34.737 --> 00:32:36.572
Okay. say it again.

384
00:32:36.656 --> 00:32:39.158
41 steps straight ahead. Then 16 steps.

385
00:32:39.241 --> 00:32:42.745
that's from the door.
fork right. 33 steps. turn right.

386
00:32:50.336 --> 00:32:51.671
Where is Stark?

387
00:32:52.463 --> 00:32:53.923
He was here a moment ago.

388
00:32:54.048 --> 00:32:55.132
Go look for him.

389
00:33:10.564 --> 00:33:13.442
Yinsen! Yinsen! Stark!

390
00:33:13.943 --> 00:33:15.569
Say something.
Say something back to him.

391
00:33:15.653 --> 00:33:18.030
- He's speaking Hungarian. I don't...
- Then speak Hungarian.

392
00:33:18.114 --> 00:33:20.616
- Okay. I know.
- What do you know?

393
00:33:43.889 --> 00:33:46.016
- How'd that work?
- Oh. my goodness.

394
00:33:46.434 --> 00:33:48.060
- It worked all right.
- That's what I do.

395
00:33:48.144 --> 00:33:50.771
- Let me finish this.
- Initialize the power sequence.

396
00:33:51.147 --> 00:33:52.148
Okay.

397
00:33:53.190 --> 00:33:54.400
- Now!
- Tell me. Tell me.

398
00:33:54.483 --> 00:33:58.112
Function 11.
Tell me when you see a progress bar.

399
00:33:58.487 --> 00:33:59.739
- It should be up right now.
- Yes.

400
00:33:59.822 --> 00:34:00.948
Talk to me. Tell me when you see it.

401
00:34:01.031 --> 00:34:02.575
- I have it.
- Press Control "I".

402
00:34:02.658 --> 00:34:05.077
- "I." Got it.
- "I." "Enter." "I" and "Enter."

403
00:34:05.161 --> 00:34:06.912
Come over here and button me up.

404
00:34:09.957 --> 00:34:11.125
Okay. All right.

405
00:34:11.208 --> 00:34:12.543
Every other hex bolt.

406
00:34:12.626 --> 00:34:14.754
- They're coming!
- Nothing pretty. just get it done.

407
00:34:14.837 --> 00:34:16.213
- Just get it done.
- They're coming.

408
00:34:18.674 --> 00:34:20.926
Make sure the checkpoints are clear
before you follow me out. okay?

409
00:34:21.010 --> 00:34:22.762
We need more time.

410
00:34:23.971 --> 00:34:24.972
Hey.

411
00:34:25.765 --> 00:34:29.059
- I'm gonna go buy you some time.
- Stick to the plan!

412
00:34:29.769 --> 00:34:31.187
Stick to the plan!

413
00:34:33.105 --> 00:34:34.356
Yinsen!

414
00:37:27.029 --> 00:37:29.490
- Yinsen!
- Watch out!

415
00:37:44.546 --> 00:37:45.714
Stark.

416
00:37:47.049 --> 00:37:49.134
Come on. We got to go.

417
00:37:49.885 --> 00:37:52.763
Move for me. come on. We got a plan.
We're gonna stick to it.

418
00:37:52.846 --> 00:37:54.765
This was always the plan. Stark.

419
00:37:55.224 --> 00:37:57.393
Come on. you're gonna go
see your family. Get up.

420
00:37:58.894 --> 00:38:00.813
My family is dead.

421
00:38:01.605 --> 00:38:03.899
I'm going to see them now. Stark.

422
00:38:06.360 --> 00:38:07.778
It's okay.

423
00:38:09.863 --> 00:38:12.866
I want this. I want this.

424
00:38:18.872 --> 00:38:20.791
Thank you for saving me.

425
00:38:22.251 --> 00:38:26.255
Don't waste it. Don't waste your life.

426
00:39:05.294 --> 00:39:06.295
My turn.

427
00:40:49.898 --> 00:40:50.899
Not bad.

428
00:41:22.890 --> 00:41:24.224
Hey!

429
00:41:46.788 --> 00:41:48.707
How was the "fun-vee"?

430
00:41:51.001 --> 00:41:53.420
Next time. you ride with me. okay?

431
00:42:24.493 --> 00:42:26.245
Watch it. coming up here.

432
00:42:28.205 --> 00:42:31.333
Are you kidding me with this?
Get rid of them.

433
00:42:39.591 --> 00:42:42.970
Your eyes are red.
A few tears for your long-lost boss?

434
00:42:43.053 --> 00:42:47.683
- Tears of joy. I hate job hunting.
- Yeah. vacation's over.

435
00:42:49.393 --> 00:42:50.519
Where to. sir?

436
00:42:50.602 --> 00:42:52.229
- Take us to the hospital. please. Happy.
- No.

437
00:42:52.312 --> 00:42:53.397
No? Tony. you have to

438
00:42:53.480 --> 00:42:54.481
- go to the hospital.
- No is a complete answer.

439
00:42:54.564 --> 00:42:56.316
- The doctor has to look at you.
- I don't have to do anything.

440
00:42:56.400 --> 00:42:58.068
I've been in captivity for three months.

441
00:42:58.151 --> 00:43:01.905
There are two things I want to do.
I want an American cheeseburger.

442
00:43:01.989 --> 00:43:02.948
- and the other...
- That's enough of that.

443
00:43:03.031 --> 00:43:05.450
...Is not what you think. I want you
to call for a press conference now.

444
00:43:05.534 --> 00:43:06.785
- Call for a press conference?
- Yeah.

445
00:43:06.868 --> 00:43:09.413
- What on earth for?
- Hogan. drive. Cheeseburger first.

446
00:43:21.883 --> 00:43:23.635
Look at this!

447
00:43:25.512 --> 00:43:26.722
Tony.

448
00:43:29.057 --> 00:43:31.893
- We were going to meet at the hospital.
- No. I'm fine.

449
00:43:31.977 --> 00:43:33.395
Look at you!

450
00:43:34.146 --> 00:43:36.523
- You had to have a burger. yeah?
- Well. come on.

451
00:43:36.606 --> 00:43:39.067
- You get me one of those?
- There's only one left. I need it.

452
00:43:42.070 --> 00:43:44.865
Hey. look who's here! Yeah!

453
00:43:50.245 --> 00:43:51.705
- Miss Potts?
- Yes.

454
00:43:51.788 --> 00:43:53.040
Can I speak to you for a moment?

455
00:43:53.123 --> 00:43:56.752
I'm not part of the press conference.
but it's about to begin right now.

456
00:43:56.835 --> 00:43:58.170
I'm not a reporter.

457
00:43:58.253 --> 00:43:59.671
I'm Agent Phil Coulson.

458
00:43:59.755 --> 00:44:01.506
with the Strategic Homeland
intervention. Enforcement

459
00:44:01.590 --> 00:44:03.175
and Logistics Division.

460
00:44:03.258 --> 00:44:06.011
- That's quite a mouthful.
- I know. We're working on it.

461
00:44:06.094 --> 00:44:10.515
You know. we've been approached
already by the DOD. the FBI. the CIA...

462
00:44:10.599 --> 00:44:14.269
We're a separate division
with a more specific focus.

463
00:44:14.353 --> 00:44:18.023
We need to debrief Mr. Stark
about the circumstances of his escape.

464
00:44:18.106 --> 00:44:21.401
- I'll put something in the book. shall I?
- Thank you.

465
00:44:26.239 --> 00:44:28.784
Hey. would it be all right
if everyone sat down?

466
00:44:28.867 --> 00:44:32.287
Why don't you just sit down?
That way you can see me. and I can...

467
00:44:32.496 --> 00:44:34.581
A little less formal and...

468
00:44:39.419 --> 00:44:42.130
- What's up with the love-in?
- Don't look at me.

469
00:44:42.214 --> 00:44:44.257
I don't know what he's up to.

470
00:44:44.341 --> 00:44:46.760
- Good to see you.
- Good to see you.

471
00:44:46.843 --> 00:44:49.304
I never got to say goodbye to Dad.

472
00:44:49.513 --> 00:44:52.265
I never got to say goodbye to my father.

473
00:44:56.061 --> 00:44:57.354
There's questions
that I would have asked him.

474
00:44:57.437 --> 00:45:00.482
I would have asked him how he felt
about what this company did.

475
00:45:01.983 --> 00:45:04.861
If he was conflicted.
if he ever had doubts.

476
00:45:05.779 --> 00:45:10.075
Or maybe he was every inch the man
we all remember from the newsreels.

477
00:45:14.413 --> 00:45:16.540
I saw young Americans killed

478
00:45:17.416 --> 00:45:21.461
by the very weapons I created
to defend them and protect them.

479
00:45:22.879 --> 00:45:24.256
And I saw

480
00:45:25.465 --> 00:45:30.262
that I had become part of a system that
is comfortable with zero accountability.

481
00:45:30.345 --> 00:45:32.347
- Mr. Stark!
- Hey. Ben.

482
00:45:33.056 --> 00:45:35.058
What happened over there?

483
00:45:35.934 --> 00:45:39.604
I had my eyes opened.
I came to realize that I have more

484
00:45:39.688 --> 00:45:44.067
to offer this world
than just making things that blow up.

485
00:45:44.151 --> 00:45:47.612
And that is why. effective immediately.
I am shutting down

486
00:45:47.696 --> 00:45:51.366
the weapons manufacturing division
of Stark international

487
00:45:51.450 --> 00:45:55.454
until such a time as I can decide
what the future of the company will be.

488
00:45:55.537 --> 00:45:57.122
I think we're gonna be selling
a lot of newspapers.

489
00:45:57.205 --> 00:45:58.957
What direction it should take.
one that I'm comfortable with

490
00:45:59.040 --> 00:46:03.086
and is consistent with the highest good
for this country. as well.

491
00:46:04.421 --> 00:46:09.217
What we should take away from this
is that Tony's back!

492
00:46:09.676 --> 00:46:12.012
And he's healthier than ever.

493
00:46:12.387 --> 00:46:15.474
We're going to have
a little internal discussion

494
00:46:15.557 --> 00:46:17.976
and we'll get back to you
with the follow-up.

495
00:46:20.187 --> 00:46:22.439
- Where is he?
- He's inside.

496
00:46:33.366 --> 00:46:36.161
Well. that... That went well.

497
00:46:36.244 --> 00:46:38.663
Did I just paint a target
on the back of my head?

498
00:46:38.747 --> 00:46:41.082
Your head? What about my head?

499
00:46:41.166 --> 00:46:44.211
What do you think the over-under on
the stock drop is gonna be tomorrow?

500
00:46:44.336 --> 00:46:47.380
- Optimistically. 40 points.
- At minimum.

501
00:46:47.756 --> 00:46:48.757
Yep.

502
00:46:49.090 --> 00:46:52.344
Tony. we're a weapons manufacturer.

503
00:46:52.427 --> 00:46:55.096
Obie. I just don't want a body count
to be our only legacy.

504
00:46:55.180 --> 00:46:57.807
That's what we do. We're iron mongers.
We make weapons.

505
00:46:57.891 --> 00:46:59.017
It's my name on the side of the building.

506
00:46:59.100 --> 00:47:01.728
And what we do
keeps the world from falling into chaos.

507
00:47:01.811 --> 00:47:03.772
Not based on what I saw.

508
00:47:05.023 --> 00:47:06.024
We're not doing a good enough job.

509
00:47:06.107 --> 00:47:07.359
We can do better.
We're gonna do something else.

510
00:47:07.442 --> 00:47:10.320
Like what?
You want us to make baby bottles?

511
00:47:11.321 --> 00:47:14.574
I think we should take another look
into arc reactor technology.

512
00:47:14.658 --> 00:47:18.995
Come on.
The arc reactor. that's a publicity stunt!

513
00:47:19.329 --> 00:47:22.457
Tony. come on. We built that thing
to shut the hippies up!

514
00:47:22.541 --> 00:47:25.669
- It works.
- Yeah. as a science project.

515
00:47:26.127 --> 00:47:29.422
The arc was never cost effective.
We knew that before we built it.

516
00:47:29.506 --> 00:47:32.676
Arc reactor technology.
that's a dead end. right?

517
00:47:32.759 --> 00:47:33.927
Maybe.

518
00:47:34.344 --> 00:47:36.930
Am I right? We haven't had
a breakthrough in that in what?

519
00:47:37.013 --> 00:47:39.558
- Thirty years.
- That's what they say.

520
00:47:42.185 --> 00:47:44.396
Could you have a lousier poker face?
Just tell me. who told you?

521
00:47:44.479 --> 00:47:47.732
- Never mind who told me. Show me.
- It's Rhodey or Pepper.

522
00:47:47.816 --> 00:47:50.151
- I want to see it.
- Okay. Rhodey.

523
00:47:58.535 --> 00:48:00.036
- Okay.
- Okay?

524
00:48:03.331 --> 00:48:04.583
It works.

525
00:48:08.628 --> 00:48:12.799
Listen to me. Tony. We're a team.
Do you understand?

526
00:48:12.882 --> 00:48:16.136
There's nothing we can't do
if we stick together.

527
00:48:16.219 --> 00:48:17.637
like your father and I.

528
00:48:17.721 --> 00:48:19.514
I'm sorry I didn't give you
a heads-up. okay?

529
00:48:19.598 --> 00:48:21.182
- But if I had...
- Tony.

530
00:48:21.266 --> 00:48:24.269
Tony. no more of this
"ready. fire. aim" business.

531
00:48:24.352 --> 00:48:27.105
- You understand me?
- That was Dad's line.

532
00:48:27.689 --> 00:48:29.858
You gotta let me handle this.

533
00:48:29.941 --> 00:48:32.360
We're gonna have to play
a whole different kind of ball now.

534
00:48:32.444 --> 00:48:34.279
We're going to have
to take a lot of heat.

535
00:48:34.362 --> 00:48:37.616
I want you to promise me
that you're gonna lay low.

536
00:48:37.866 --> 00:48:39.618
Stark industries!

537
00:48:39.701 --> 00:48:42.579
I've got one recommendation!
Ready? Ready?

538
00:48:42.662 --> 00:48:43.830
Sell. sell. sell!

539
00:48:44.039 --> 00:48:45.999
Abandon ship!

540
00:48:46.082 --> 00:48:49.461
Does the Hindenburg ring any bells?

541
00:48:50.837 --> 00:48:55.759
Let me show you the new
Stark Industries business plan!

542
00:48:57.385 --> 00:49:01.348
Look. that's a weapons company
that doesn't make weapons!

543
00:49:01.890 --> 00:49:04.726
Pepper. How big are your hands?

544
00:49:05.226 --> 00:49:07.437
- What?
- How big are your hands?

545
00:49:07.520 --> 00:49:10.398
- I don't understand why...
- Get down here. I need you.

546
00:49:17.781 --> 00:49:18.865
Hey.

547
00:49:20.909 --> 00:49:23.411
Let's see them. Show me your hands.

548
00:49:23.495 --> 00:49:24.496
Let's see them.

549
00:49:24.871 --> 00:49:26.915
Oh. wow. They are small.
Very petite. indeed.

550
00:49:27.874 --> 00:49:30.418
I just need your help for a sec.

551
00:49:31.211 --> 00:49:33.380
Oh. my God. is that the thing
that's keeping you alive?

552
00:49:33.463 --> 00:49:36.049
It was. It is now an antique.

553
00:49:36.841 --> 00:49:39.636
This is what will be keeping me alive
for the foreseeable future.

554
00:49:39.719 --> 00:49:44.349
I'm swapping it up for an upgraded unit.
and I just ran into a little speed bump.

555
00:49:44.599 --> 00:49:47.352
- Speed bump. what does that mean?
- It's nothing. It's just a little snag.

556
00:49:47.435 --> 00:49:50.814
There's an exposed wire
under this device.

557
00:49:50.897 --> 00:49:54.025
And it's contacting the socket wall
and causing a little bit of a short.

558
00:49:54.109 --> 00:49:55.777
It's fine.

559
00:49:56.653 --> 00:49:58.571
- What do you want me to do?
- Put that on the table over there.

560
00:49:58.655 --> 00:50:00.448
- That is irrelevant.
- Oh. my God!

561
00:50:00.532 --> 00:50:04.828
I want you to reach in. and you're just
gonna gently lift the wire out.

562
00:50:05.620 --> 00:50:07.706
- Is it safe?
- Yeah. it should be fine.

563
00:50:07.789 --> 00:50:09.416
It's like Operation.
You just don't let it touch

564
00:50:09.499 --> 00:50:10.875
the socket wall or it goes "beep."

565
00:50:10.959 --> 00:50:13.420
- What do you mean. "Operation"?
- It's just a game. never mind.

566
00:50:13.503 --> 00:50:17.549
- Just gently lift the wire. Okay? Great.
- Okay.

567
00:50:19.384 --> 00:50:21.886
You know. I don't think
that I'm qualified to do this.

568
00:50:21.970 --> 00:50:26.015
No. you're fine.
You're the most capable. qualified.

569
00:50:26.099 --> 00:50:29.644
trustworthy person I've ever met.
You're gonna do great.

570
00:50:30.895 --> 00:50:32.856
Is it too much of a problem to ask?
'Cause I'm...

571
00:50:32.939 --> 00:50:35.608
- Okay. okay.
- I really need your help here.

572
00:50:35.692 --> 00:50:36.818
Okay.

573
00:50:41.156 --> 00:50:42.741
Oh. there's pus!

574
00:50:42.824 --> 00:50:47.454
It's not pus. It's an inorganic
plasmic discharge from the device.

575
00:50:47.537 --> 00:50:49.456
- not from my body.
- It smells!

576
00:50:49.539 --> 00:50:51.082
Yeah. it does.

577
00:50:51.458 --> 00:50:54.127
The copper wire.
The copper wire. you got it?

578
00:50:54.210 --> 00:50:55.336
- Okay. I got it! I got it!
- Okay. you got it?

579
00:50:55.420 --> 00:50:58.339
Now. don't let it touch the sides
when you're coming out!

580
00:50:58.423 --> 00:50:59.424
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

581
00:50:59.507 --> 00:51:00.842
That's what
I was trying to tell you before.

582
00:51:00.925 --> 00:51:03.094
Okay. now make sure
that when you pull it out. you don't...

583
00:51:03.178 --> 00:51:06.097
There's a magnet at the end of it!
That was it. You just pulled it out.

584
00:51:06.181 --> 00:51:07.348
- Oh. God!
- Okay. I was not expecting...

585
00:51:07.432 --> 00:51:09.601
- Don't put it back in! Don't put it back in!
- Okay. what do I do?

586
00:51:09.684 --> 00:51:10.685
What's wrong?

587
00:51:10.769 --> 00:51:12.145
Nothing.
I'm just going into cardiac arrest

588
00:51:12.228 --> 00:51:13.521
'cause you yanked it out like a trout...

589
00:51:13.605 --> 00:51:16.357
- What? You said it was safe!
- We gotta hurry. Take this. Take this.

590
00:51:16.441 --> 00:51:18.443
- You gotta switch it out really quick.
- Okay. Okay.

591
00:51:18.735 --> 00:51:20.570
- Tony? It's going to be okay.
- What?

592
00:51:20.653 --> 00:51:21.613
- Is it?
- It's gonna be okay.

593
00:51:21.696 --> 00:51:24.365
- I'm gonna make this okay.
- Let's hope.

594
00:51:24.866 --> 00:51:29.037
Okay. you're gonna attach that
to the base plate. Make sure you...

595
00:51:33.082 --> 00:51:36.628
Was that so hard? That was fun. right?
Here. I got it. I got it. Here.

596
00:51:37.796 --> 00:51:38.838
Nice.

597
00:51:38.922 --> 00:51:41.174
- Are you okay?
- Yeah. I feel great.

598
00:51:41.257 --> 00:51:42.550
You okay?

599
00:51:43.968 --> 00:51:46.846
Don't ever. ever. ever.

600
00:51:46.930 --> 00:51:49.933
ever ask me to do
anything like that ever again.

601
00:51:50.016 --> 00:51:52.143
I don't have anyone but you.

602
00:51:57.774 --> 00:51:58.775
Anyway...

603
00:52:04.656 --> 00:52:07.575
- What do you want me to do with this?
- That?

604
00:52:08.409 --> 00:52:09.744
Destroy it.

605
00:52:10.286 --> 00:52:11.788
Incinerate it.

606
00:52:12.455 --> 00:52:14.082
You don't want to keep it?

607
00:52:14.165 --> 00:52:18.336
Pepper. I've been called many things.
"Nostalgic" is not one of them.

608
00:52:18.878 --> 00:52:22.590
- Will that be all. Mr. Stark?
- That will be all. Miss Potts.

609
00:52:23.258 --> 00:52:25.009
Hey. Butterfingers. come here.

610
00:52:25.093 --> 00:52:27.011
What's all this stuff
doing on top of my desk?

611
00:52:27.095 --> 00:52:30.306
That's my phone.
that's a picture of me and my dad.

612
00:52:30.390 --> 00:52:33.309
Right there. In the garbage.
All that stuff.

613
00:52:39.482 --> 00:52:43.778
The future of air combat.
Is it manned or unmanned?

614
00:52:44.070 --> 00:52:46.197
I'll tell you. in my experience.

615
00:52:46.281 --> 00:52:51.035
no unmanned aerial vehicle
will ever trump a pilot's instinct.

616
00:52:51.411 --> 00:52:52.662
his insight.

617
00:52:52.745 --> 00:52:55.748
that ability to look
into a situation beyond the obvious

618
00:52:55.832 --> 00:52:59.460
and discern its outcome.
or a pilot's judgment.

619
00:52:59.544 --> 00:53:02.547
Colonel?
Why not a pilot without the plane?

620
00:53:02.630 --> 00:53:04.632
Look who fell out of the sky.
Mr. Tony Stark.

621
00:53:04.716 --> 00:53:06.634
- Hello. sir.
- Speaking of manned or unmanned.

622
00:53:06.718 --> 00:53:08.553
you gotta get him to tell you
about the time he guessed wrong

623
00:53:08.636 --> 00:53:11.264
at spring break.
Just remember that. spring break. 1987.

624
00:53:11.347 --> 00:53:12.640
- That lovely lady you woke up with.
- Don't do that!

625
00:53:12.724 --> 00:53:14.100
- What was his name?
- Don't do that.

626
00:53:14.183 --> 00:53:15.268
- Was it Ivan?
- Don't do that.

627
00:53:15.351 --> 00:53:16.603
They'll believe it. Don't do that.

628
00:53:16.686 --> 00:53:17.854
- Okay.
- Don't do that.

629
00:53:17.937 --> 00:53:20.899
- Pleasure meeting you.
- Give us a couple minutes. you guys.

630
00:53:23.818 --> 00:53:25.486
- I'm surprised.
- Why?

631
00:53:25.570 --> 00:53:28.323
I swear. I didn't expect to see you
walking around so soon.

632
00:53:28.448 --> 00:53:30.241
I'm doing a little better than walking.

633
00:53:30.325 --> 00:53:31.826
- Really?
- Yeah.

634
00:53:32.493 --> 00:53:35.163
Rhodey. I'm working on something big.

635
00:53:35.330 --> 00:53:38.249
I came to talk to you.
I want you to be a part of it.

636
00:53:39.500 --> 00:53:41.961
You're about to make a whole
lot of people around here real happy.

637
00:53:42.045 --> 00:53:45.048
'cause that little stunt
at the press conference.

638
00:53:45.131 --> 00:53:46.716
that was a doozy.

639
00:53:47.091 --> 00:53:51.596
This is not for the military. I'm not...
It's different.

640
00:53:51.679 --> 00:53:54.349
What? You're a humanitarian now
or something?

641
00:53:54.432 --> 00:53:55.850
- I need you to listen to me.
- No.

642
00:53:55.934 --> 00:53:59.854
What you need is time
to get your mind right.

643
00:54:01.689 --> 00:54:03.274
- I'm serious.
- Okay.

644
00:54:06.235 --> 00:54:08.404
It's nice seeing you. Tony.

645
00:54:08.488 --> 00:54:09.697
Thanks.

646
00:54:17.914 --> 00:54:21.334
- Jarvis. you up?
- For you. sir. always.

647
00:54:21.584 --> 00:54:25.505
I'd like to open a new project file.
index as Mark ll.

648
00:54:26.673 --> 00:54:30.385
Shall I store this on
the Stark industries Central Database?

649
00:54:30.677 --> 00:54:33.054
Actually. I don't know
who to trust right now.

650
00:54:33.137 --> 00:54:35.974
Till further notice. why don't we just
keep everything on my private server?

651
00:54:36.057 --> 00:54:38.768
Working on a secret project.
are we. sir?

652
00:54:42.730 --> 00:54:45.817
I don't want this winding up
in the wrong hands.

653
00:54:47.944 --> 00:54:50.446
Maybe in mine.
it can actually do some good.

654
00:55:33.698 --> 00:55:36.451
Next. Up.

655
00:55:37.076 --> 00:55:39.954
Not in the boot. Dummy. Right here.
You got me?

656
00:55:40.038 --> 00:55:42.123
Stay put. Nice.

657
00:55:43.958 --> 00:55:47.795
You're of no benefit at all.
Move down to the toe. I got this.

658
00:55:48.254 --> 00:55:50.423
Okay. I'm sorry. am I in your way?

659
00:55:57.305 --> 00:55:58.473
Up.

660
00:55:59.307 --> 00:56:01.142
Screw it. Don't even move.

661
00:56:01.225 --> 00:56:04.312
You are a tragedy.

662
00:56:14.155 --> 00:56:16.741
Okay. let's do this right.

663
00:56:17.408 --> 00:56:20.244
Start mark. half a meter.
and back and center.

664
00:56:22.997 --> 00:56:25.208
Dummy. look alive.
You're on standby for fire safety.

665
00:56:25.291 --> 00:56:26.709
You. roll it.

666
00:56:29.045 --> 00:56:32.590
Okay. Activate hand controls.

667
00:56:36.928 --> 00:56:38.096
We're gonna start off nice and easy.

668
00:56:38.179 --> 00:56:41.349
We're gonna see if
10% thrust capacity achieves lift.

669
00:56:41.432 --> 00:56:42.809
And three.

670
00:56:43.643 --> 00:56:44.685
two.

671
00:56:45.478 --> 00:56:46.604
one.

672
00:57:23.683 --> 00:57:25.977
Up two. All right. set that.

673
00:57:26.060 --> 00:57:28.479
I've been buzzing you.
Did you hear the intercom?

674
00:57:28.563 --> 00:57:30.398
Yeah. everything's... What?

675
00:57:30.481 --> 00:57:31.649
- Obadiah's upstairs.
- Great!

676
00:57:31.732 --> 00:57:33.734
- What would you like me to tell him?
- Great. I'll be right up.

677
00:57:34.235 --> 00:57:35.444
Okay.

678
00:57:36.237 --> 00:57:38.030
I thought you said
you were done making weapons.

679
00:57:38.114 --> 00:57:39.115
It is.

680
00:57:39.615 --> 00:57:43.202
This is a flight stabilizer.
It's completely harmless.

681
00:57:47.248 --> 00:57:48.457
I didn't expect that.

682
00:57:53.754 --> 00:57:55.173
How'd it go?

683
00:57:57.425 --> 00:57:59.093
It went that bad. huh?

684
00:57:59.177 --> 00:58:01.846
Just because I brought pizza
back from New York

685
00:58:01.929 --> 00:58:05.808
- doesn't mean it went bad.
- Sure doesn't. Oh. boy.

686
00:58:05.892 --> 00:58:08.769
It would have gone better
if you were there.

687
00:58:09.020 --> 00:58:10.563
You told me to lay low.
That's what I've been doing.

688
00:58:10.646 --> 00:58:15.193
- I lay low. and you take care of all...
- Hey. come on. In public. The press.

689
00:58:16.277 --> 00:58:20.448
- This was a board of directors meeting.
- This was a board of directors meeting?

690
00:58:21.490 --> 00:58:23.951
The board is claiming
you have posttraumatic stress.

691
00:58:24.035 --> 00:58:25.161
They're filing an injunction.

692
00:58:25.244 --> 00:58:27.288
- A what?
- They want to lock you out.

693
00:58:27.371 --> 00:58:28.581
Why. 'cause the stocks
dipped 40 points?

694
00:58:28.664 --> 00:58:29.665
We knew that was gonna happen.

695
00:58:29.749 --> 00:58:31.834
- Fifty-six and a half.
- It doesn't matter.

696
00:58:31.918 --> 00:58:34.128
We own the controlling interest
in the company.

697
00:58:34.212 --> 00:58:36.964
Tony. the board has rights. too.

698
00:58:37.840 --> 00:58:41.719
They're making the case
that you and your new direction

699
00:58:41.802 --> 00:58:44.055
- isn't in the company's best interest.
- I'm being responsible!

700
00:58:44.138 --> 00:58:47.141
That's a new direction for me.
for the company.

701
00:58:48.059 --> 00:58:51.938
I mean. me on the company's behalf
being responsible for the way that...

702
00:58:52.021 --> 00:58:53.064
This is great.

703
00:58:53.147 --> 00:58:56.609
- Oh. come on. Tony. Tony.
- I'll be in the shop.

704
00:58:56.692 --> 00:58:58.903
Hey. hey! Hey. Tony. Listen.

705
00:58:58.986 --> 00:59:02.323
I'm trying to turn this thing around.
but you gotta give me something.

706
00:59:02.406 --> 00:59:03.991
Something to pitch them.

707
00:59:04.116 --> 00:59:07.578
Let me have the engineers analyze that.
You know. draw up some specs.

708
00:59:07.662 --> 00:59:09.789
- No. No. absolutely not.
- It'll give me a bone to throw the boys

709
00:59:09.872 --> 00:59:11.457
- in New York!
- This one stays with me.

710
00:59:11.540 --> 00:59:14.377
- That's it. Obie. Forget it.
- All right. well. this stays with me. then.

711
00:59:14.460 --> 00:59:16.295
Go on. here. you can have a piece.

712
00:59:16.379 --> 00:59:17.880
- Take two.
- Thank you.

713
00:59:17.964 --> 00:59:19.840
You mind if I come down there
and see what you're doing?

714
00:59:19.924 --> 00:59:21.550
Good night. Obie.

715
00:59:22.176 --> 00:59:27.014
Day 11. test 37. configuration 2.0.
For lack of a better option.

716
00:59:27.098 --> 00:59:29.767
Dummy is still on fire safety.
If you douse me again.

717
00:59:29.850 --> 00:59:32.687
and I'm not on fire.
I'm donating you to a city college.

718
00:59:32.770 --> 00:59:34.605
All right. nice and easy.

719
00:59:34.689 --> 00:59:39.652
Seriously. just gonna start off
with 1% thrust capacity.

720
00:59:41.153 --> 00:59:43.239
And three. two. one.

721
00:59:55.042 --> 00:59:56.085
Okay.

722
00:59:57.378 --> 00:59:59.005
Please don't follow me around
with it. either.

723
00:59:59.088 --> 01:00:01.507
'cause I feel like I'm gonna
catch on fire spontaneously.

724
01:00:01.590 --> 01:00:03.301
Just stand down!
If something happens. then come in.

725
01:00:03.384 --> 01:00:05.636
And again. let's bring it up to 2.5.

726
01:00:05.720 --> 01:00:07.346
Three. two. one.

727
01:00:23.904 --> 01:00:26.490
Okay. this is where I don't want to be!

728
01:00:26.574 --> 01:00:27.908
Not the car. not the car!

729
01:00:29.243 --> 01:00:30.244
Table!

730
01:00:41.339 --> 01:00:45.468
Could be worse! Could be worse!
We're fine! Okay.

731
01:01:03.569 --> 01:01:05.112
No!

732
01:01:07.156 --> 01:01:08.824
Yeah. I can fly.

733
01:01:13.621 --> 01:01:16.540
- Jarvis. are you there?
- At your service. sir.

734
01:01:16.624 --> 01:01:18.876
- Engage Heads Up Display.
- Check.

735
01:01:18.959 --> 01:01:21.003
Import all preferences
from home interface.

736
01:01:21.087 --> 01:01:22.546
Will do. sir.

737
01:01:29.470 --> 01:01:30.513
All right. what do you say?

738
01:01:30.596 --> 01:01:34.100
I have indeed been uploaded. sir.
We're online and ready.

739
01:01:34.183 --> 01:01:35.810
Can we start the virtual walk-around?

740
01:01:35.893 --> 01:01:38.896
Importing preferences
and calibrating virtual environment.

741
01:01:38.979 --> 01:01:40.272
Do a check on control surfaces.

742
01:01:40.356 --> 01:01:41.899
As you wish.

743
01:02:03.796 --> 01:02:06.340
Test complete. Preparing to
power down and begin diagnostics.

744
01:02:06.424 --> 01:02:09.343
Yeah. Tell you what.
Do a weather and ATC check.

745
01:02:09.427 --> 01:02:10.928
Start listening in on ground control.

746
01:02:11.011 --> 01:02:12.096
Sir. there are still terabytes

747
01:02:12.179 --> 01:02:14.765
of calculations needed
before an actual flight is...

748
01:02:14.849 --> 01:02:18.769
Jarvis! Sometimes you got to run
before you can walk.

749
01:02:18.853 --> 01:02:23.190
Ready? In three. two. one.

750
01:02:46.464 --> 01:02:48.257
Handles like a dream.

751
01:03:16.327 --> 01:03:17.953
All right. let's see what
this thing can do.

752
01:03:18.037 --> 01:03:19.455
What's SR-71's record?

753
01:03:19.538 --> 01:03:23.334
The altitude record for fixed wing flight
is 85.000 feet. sir.

754
01:03:23.751 --> 01:03:26.420
Records are made to be broken!
Come on!

755
01:03:29.590 --> 01:03:33.219
Sir. there is a potentially fatal
buildup of ice occurring.

756
01:03:33.302 --> 01:03:34.428
Keep going!

757
01:03:36.680 --> 01:03:38.015
Higher!

758
01:03:51.654 --> 01:03:55.950
We iced up. Jarvis!
Deploy flaps! Jarvis!

759
01:03:58.702 --> 01:04:01.080
Come on. we got to break the ice!

760
01:04:36.323 --> 01:04:37.575
Kill power.

761
01:06:01.784 --> 01:06:05.162
Notes. Main transducer feels sluggish
at plus 40 altitude.

762
01:06:05.245 --> 01:06:09.667
Hull pressurization is problematic.
I'm thinking icing is the probable factor.

763
01:06:09.750 --> 01:06:12.002
A very astute observation. sir.

764
01:06:12.086 --> 01:06:13.837
Perhaps. if you intend
to visit other planets.

765
01:06:13.921 --> 01:06:15.381
we should improve the exosystems.

766
01:06:15.464 --> 01:06:18.050
Connect to the sys. co.
Have it reconfigure the shell metals.

767
01:06:18.133 --> 01:06:21.220
Use the gold titanium alloy from
the seraphim tactical satellite.

768
01:06:21.303 --> 01:06:25.182
That should ensure a fuselage integrity
while maintaining power-to-weight ratio.

769
01:06:25.265 --> 01:06:26.517
- Got it?
- Yes.

770
01:06:26.600 --> 01:06:28.936
Shall I render
using proposed specifications?

771
01:06:29.019 --> 01:06:30.396
Thrill me.

772
01:06:31.772 --> 01:06:36.318
Tonight's red-hot red carpet is right
here at the Disney Concert Hall.

773
01:06:36.402 --> 01:06:40.656
where Tony Stark's third annual benefit
for the Firefighter's Family Fund

774
01:06:40.739 --> 01:06:42.324
has become the place to be
for L.A.'s high society.

775
01:06:42.408 --> 01:06:43.659
Jarvis. we get an invite for that?

776
01:06:43.742 --> 01:06:46.245
I have no record of an invitation. sir.

777
01:06:46.328 --> 01:06:47.788
...Hasn't been seen in public

778
01:06:47.871 --> 01:06:51.625
since his bizarre and highly
controversial press conference.

779
01:06:51.792 --> 01:06:54.461
Some claim he's suffering
from posttraumatic stress

780
01:06:54.545 --> 01:06:58.173
and has been bedridden for weeks.
Whatever the case may be.

781
01:06:58.632 --> 01:07:01.385
no one expects an appearance
from him tonight.

782
01:07:01.468 --> 01:07:03.637
The render is complete.

783
01:07:03.721 --> 01:07:05.389
A little ostentatious. don't you think?

784
01:07:05.472 --> 01:07:08.559
What was I thinking?
You're usually so discreet.

785
01:07:10.185 --> 01:07:12.813
Tell you what.
Throw a little hot-rod red in there.

786
01:07:12.896 --> 01:07:15.816
Yes. that should help you
keep a low profile.

787
01:07:18.986 --> 01:07:20.863
The render is complete.

788
01:07:21.321 --> 01:07:23.240
Hey. I like it. Fabricate it. Paint it.

789
01:07:23.323 --> 01:07:24.908
Commencing automated assembly.

790
01:07:24.992 --> 01:07:28.162
Estimated completion time is five hours.

791
01:07:28.245 --> 01:07:29.371
Don't wait up for me. honey.

792
01:07:53.562 --> 01:07:57.316
Weapons manufacturing is only
one small part of what Stark industries

793
01:07:57.399 --> 01:08:01.195
is all about. and our partnership
with the fire and rescue community...

794
01:08:03.822 --> 01:08:06.366
- Hey. Tony. remember me?
- Sure don't.

795
01:08:07.868 --> 01:08:09.369
You look great. Hef.

796
01:08:11.205 --> 01:08:12.498
We're going to have a great quarter.

797
01:08:12.581 --> 01:08:16.335
What's the world coming to when
a guy's got to crash his own party?

798
01:08:16.418 --> 01:08:20.631
Look at you. Hey. what a surprise.

799
01:08:20.714 --> 01:08:22.466
I'll see you inside.

800
01:08:23.050 --> 01:08:26.303
Hey. Listen. take it slow. all right?

801
01:08:26.386 --> 01:08:28.138
I think I got the board
right where we want them.

802
01:08:28.222 --> 01:08:31.809
You got it. Just cabin fever.
I'll just be a minute.

803
01:08:36.313 --> 01:08:39.900
- Give me a Scotch. I'm starving.
- Mr. Stark?

804
01:08:40.567 --> 01:08:42.361
- Yeah?
- Agent Coulson.

805
01:08:42.820 --> 01:08:45.030
Oh. yeah. yeah. yeah.
The guy from the...

806
01:08:45.113 --> 01:08:48.450
Strategic Homeland intervention.
Enforcement and Logistics Division.

807
01:08:48.534 --> 01:08:50.160
God. you need a new name for that.

808
01:08:50.244 --> 01:08:52.246
Yeah. I hear that a lot.

809
01:08:53.038 --> 01:08:56.834
Listen. I know this must be a trying time
for you. but we need to debrief you.

810
01:08:56.917 --> 01:08:58.877
There's still
a lot of unanswered questions.

811
01:08:58.961 --> 01:09:00.838
and time can be a factor
with these things.

812
01:09:00.921 --> 01:09:02.965
Let's just put something on the books.

813
01:09:03.048 --> 01:09:06.426
How about the 24th at 7:00 p.m.
at Stark industries?

814
01:09:06.760 --> 01:09:10.055
Tell you what.
You got it. You're absolutely right.

815
01:09:10.264 --> 01:09:14.476
Well. I'm going to go to my assistant.
and we'll make a date.

816
01:09:15.936 --> 01:09:18.021
You look fantastic!
I didn't recognize you.

817
01:09:18.105 --> 01:09:20.357
- What are you doing here?
- Just avoiding government agents.

818
01:09:20.440 --> 01:09:22.234
- Are you by yourself?
- Yes. Where'd you get that dress?

819
01:09:22.317 --> 01:09:24.152
- Oh. it was a birthday present.
- That's great.

820
01:09:24.236 --> 01:09:26.363
- From you. actually.
- Well. I got great taste.

821
01:09:26.446 --> 01:09:27.698
Yes.

822
01:09:27.781 --> 01:09:29.700
- You want to dance?
- Oh. no.

823
01:09:29.783 --> 01:09:32.286
- All right. come on.
- Thank you. No.

824
01:09:42.713 --> 01:09:44.965
Am I making you uncomfortable?

825
01:09:45.340 --> 01:09:50.596
No. No. I always forget to wear
deodorant and dance with my boss

826
01:09:50.679 --> 01:09:54.516
in front of everyone that I work with
in a dress with no back.

827
01:09:54.808 --> 01:09:57.352
- You look great and you smell great.
- Oh. God.

828
01:09:57.436 --> 01:09:59.313
But I could fire you if that would
take the edge off.

829
01:09:59.396 --> 01:10:03.066
I actually don't think that
you could tie your shoes without me.

830
01:10:03.150 --> 01:10:04.568
- I'd make it a week. Sure.
- Really?

831
01:10:04.651 --> 01:10:07.154
What's your Social Security number?

832
01:10:10.657 --> 01:10:12.409
- Five.
- Five?

833
01:10:13.243 --> 01:10:14.536
- Right.
- Right.

834
01:10:14.620 --> 01:10:16.955
You're missing just
a couple of digits there.

835
01:10:17.039 --> 01:10:20.250
The other eight?
So I got you for the other eight.

836
01:10:32.846 --> 01:10:35.891
- How about a little air?
- Yes. I need some air.

837
01:10:37.851 --> 01:10:39.770
- That was totally weird.
- Totally harmless.

838
01:10:39.853 --> 01:10:42.689
It was totally not harmless. by the way.

839
01:10:42.856 --> 01:10:44.149
We're dancing. No one's even watching.

840
01:10:44.232 --> 01:10:46.026
Everybody who I work with...
No. you know why?

841
01:10:46.109 --> 01:10:49.279
I think you lost objectivity. I think
they just... People... We just danced.

842
01:10:49.363 --> 01:10:52.741
No. it was not just a dance. You don't
understand because you're you.

843
01:10:52.824 --> 01:10:55.619
And everybody knows
exactly who you are

844
01:10:55.702 --> 01:10:58.956
and how you are with girls
and all of that. which is completely fine.

845
01:10:59.039 --> 01:11:01.416
But. you know. then me. you're my boss.

846
01:11:01.500 --> 01:11:03.460
- and I'm dancing with you.
- I don't think it was taken that way.

847
01:11:03.543 --> 01:11:06.421
Because it makes me look like
the one who's trying to...

848
01:11:06.505 --> 01:11:08.423
- I just think you're overstating it.
- You know. and we're here.

849
01:11:08.507 --> 01:11:12.302
and then I'm wearing this ridiculous

850
01:11:12.386 --> 01:11:15.138
dress. and then we were dancing
like that and...

851
01:11:29.069 --> 01:11:31.989
- I would like a drink. please.
- Got it. okay.

852
01:11:33.365 --> 01:11:36.284
- I would like a vodka martini. please.
- Okay.

853
01:11:36.368 --> 01:11:41.081
Very dry with olives. a lot of olives.
Like. at least three olives.

854
01:11:41.915 --> 01:11:45.002
Two vodka martinis. extra dry.
extra olives. extra fast.

855
01:11:45.085 --> 01:11:47.254
Make one of them dirty. will you?

856
01:11:51.883 --> 01:11:54.469
Wow. Tony Stark.

857
01:11:54.803 --> 01:11:57.139
- Oh. hey.
- Fancy seeing you here.

858
01:12:01.184 --> 01:12:02.185
- Carrie.
- Christine.

859
01:12:02.269 --> 01:12:03.270
That's right.

860
01:12:03.353 --> 01:12:06.023
You have a lot of nerve
showing up here tonight.

861
01:12:06.106 --> 01:12:07.524
Can I at least get a reaction from you?

862
01:12:07.607 --> 01:12:10.027
Panic. I would say panic is my reaction.

863
01:12:10.110 --> 01:12:11.486
'Cause I was referring
to your company's

864
01:12:11.570 --> 01:12:12.904
involvement in this latest atrocity.

865
01:12:12.988 --> 01:12:15.532
Yeah. They just put my name on the
invitation. I don't know what to tell you.

866
01:12:15.615 --> 01:12:17.993
I actually almost bought it.
hook. line and sinker.

867
01:12:18.076 --> 01:12:20.454
I was out of town for a couple months.
in case you didn't hear.

868
01:12:20.537 --> 01:12:22.873
Is this what you call accountability?

869
01:12:22.956 --> 01:12:25.667
It's a town called Gulmira. Heard of it?

870
01:12:37.220 --> 01:12:39.639
- When were these taken?
- Yesterday.

871
01:12:40.140 --> 01:12:42.142
- I didn't approve any shipment.
- Well. your company did.

872
01:12:42.225 --> 01:12:44.186
Well. I'm not my company.

873
01:12:45.312 --> 01:12:48.565
- Please. do you mind?
- Have you seen these pictures?

874
01:12:48.648 --> 01:12:49.983
- What's going on in Gulmira?
- Tony. Tony.

875
01:12:50.067 --> 01:12:53.403
- You can't afford to be this naive.
- You know what? I was naive before.

876
01:12:53.487 --> 01:12:55.322
when they said.
"Here's the line. We don't cross it."

877
01:12:55.405 --> 01:12:56.782
"This is how we do business."

878
01:12:56.865 --> 01:13:00.077
if we're double-dealing under the table...
Are we?

879
01:13:00.494 --> 01:13:02.662
Tony. your picture. please!

880
01:13:04.873 --> 01:13:08.376
Let's take a picture. Come on.
Picture time!

881
01:13:10.170 --> 01:13:13.298
Tony. Who do you think locked you out?

882
01:13:14.007 --> 01:13:17.302
I was the one who filed
the injunction against you.

883
01:13:19.721 --> 01:13:22.474
It was the only way I could protect you.

884
01:13:24.851 --> 01:13:26.061
No. No.

885
01:13:34.111 --> 01:13:38.406
The 15-mile hike to the outskirts
of Gulmira can only be described

886
01:13:38.490 --> 01:13:42.202
as a descent into hell.
into a modern day Heart of Darkness.

887
01:13:42.369 --> 01:13:45.288
Simple farmers and herders
from peaceful villages

888
01:13:45.372 --> 01:13:47.082
have been driven from their homes.

889
01:13:47.165 --> 01:13:51.419
displaced from their lands by warlords
emboldened by a new-found power.

890
01:13:51.711 --> 01:13:54.756
Villagers have been forced to take
shelter in whatever crude dwellings

891
01:13:54.840 --> 01:13:57.634
they can find in the ruins
of other villages.

892
01:13:57.717 --> 01:14:01.555
or here in the remnants
of an old Soviet smelting plant.

893
01:14:06.351 --> 01:14:09.729
Recent violence has been attributed
to a group of foreign fighters

894
01:14:09.813 --> 01:14:12.566
referred to by locals as the Ten Rings.

895
01:14:12.774 --> 01:14:16.153
As you can see. these men are
heavily armed and on a mission.

896
01:14:16.236 --> 01:14:20.365
A mission that could prove fatal
to anyone who stands in their way.

897
01:14:20.574 --> 01:14:23.118
With no political will
or international pressure.

898
01:14:23.201 --> 01:14:25.662
there's very little hope
for these refugees.

899
01:14:25.745 --> 01:14:28.999
Around me. a woman begging for news
on her husband.

900
01:14:29.082 --> 01:14:30.876
who was kidnapped by insurgents.

901
01:14:30.959 --> 01:14:33.545
either forced to join their militia...

902
01:14:34.546 --> 01:14:37.174
Desperate refugees clutch
yellowed photographs.

903
01:14:37.257 --> 01:14:39.843
holding them up to anyone
who will stop.

904
01:14:39.926 --> 01:14:43.555
A child's simple question.
"Where are my mother and father?"

905
01:14:45.140 --> 01:14:47.559
There's very little hope
for these refugees.

906
01:14:47.642 --> 01:14:51.521
refugees who can only wonder who.
if anyone. will help.

907
01:16:24.489 --> 01:16:25.657
Hurry it up.

908
01:16:25.740 --> 01:16:26.950
Put the women in the trucks.

909
01:16:27.033 --> 01:16:28.076
Stack the weapons here.

910
01:16:28.159 --> 01:16:29.160
Clear all the houses.

911
01:16:29.244 --> 01:16:30.912
That one there.
Faster. Faster.

912
01:16:39.087 --> 01:16:40.088
Grab that dog.

913
01:16:43.049 --> 01:16:45.176
Put him with the others.

914
01:16:56.021 --> 01:16:57.397
What the hell is this?

915
01:17:09.034 --> 01:17:10.910
Shoot this dog.

916
01:17:11.077 --> 01:17:12.662
You're all incompetent.

917
01:17:15.957 --> 01:17:17.000
Turn your head.

918
01:18:23.775 --> 01:18:25.485
He's all yours.

919
01:19:24.294 --> 01:19:26.296
What the hell was that?
Were we cleared to go in there?

920
01:19:26.379 --> 01:19:28.465
No. they were using human shields.
We never got the green light.

921
01:19:28.548 --> 01:19:30.258
Put me through to State.
They're going to be all over this.

922
01:19:30.341 --> 01:19:32.010
Get those monitors up!

923
01:19:32.093 --> 01:19:33.428
We got a bogey!

924
01:19:33.511 --> 01:19:35.638
- Wasn't Air Force!
- We got the CIA on the line?

925
01:19:35.722 --> 01:19:37.682
I've got Langley on the line.
They want to know if it's us.

926
01:19:37.765 --> 01:19:39.434
No. it definitely is not us. sir!

927
01:19:39.517 --> 01:19:41.186
- It wasn't Navy.
- Wasn't Marines.

928
01:19:41.269 --> 01:19:43.771
I need answers!
Can I please get eyes on target?

929
01:19:43.855 --> 01:19:46.107
- Negative. negative.
- Cannot identify.

930
01:19:46.232 --> 01:19:48.860
Get me Colonel Rhodes from
Weapons Development down here now!

931
01:19:55.658 --> 01:19:57.410
We ran an ID check
and cross-referenced

932
01:19:57.494 --> 01:19:59.204
with all known databases.
We have nothing.

933
01:19:59.287 --> 01:20:01.498
Any high altitude surveillance
in the region?

934
01:20:01.581 --> 01:20:03.291
We got an AWAC
and a Global Hawk in the area.

935
01:20:03.374 --> 01:20:05.043
So this thing just appeared
out of nowhere?

936
01:20:05.126 --> 01:20:06.503
How come it didn't show up
on the radar?

937
01:20:06.586 --> 01:20:08.546
Got a minimal radar cross-section. sir.

938
01:20:08.630 --> 01:20:10.798
- Is it stealth?
- No. sir. it's tiny.

939
01:20:10.924 --> 01:20:13.259
We think it's an unmanned
aerial vehicle.

940
01:20:13.343 --> 01:20:15.178
Colonel. what are we dealing with here?

941
01:20:17.722 --> 01:20:20.683
- Let me make a call.
- Sergeant. clear a hole.

942
01:20:24.229 --> 01:20:26.022
- Hello?
- Tony?

943
01:20:26.105 --> 01:20:27.857
- Who's this?
- It's Rhodes.

944
01:20:28.107 --> 01:20:30.193
- Sorry. hello?
- I said it's Rhodes.

945
01:20:30.276 --> 01:20:33.154
- Speak up. please.
- What in the hell is that noise?

946
01:20:33.238 --> 01:20:36.699
- Oh. yeah. I'm driving with the top down.
- Yeah. well. I need your help right now.

947
01:20:36.783 --> 01:20:38.159
It's funny how that works. huh?

948
01:20:38.243 --> 01:20:41.621
Yeah. Speaking of funny. we've got a
weapons depot that was just blown up

949
01:20:41.704 --> 01:20:43.373
a few clicks from where
you were being held captive.

950
01:20:43.456 --> 01:20:45.083
Well. that's a hot spot.

951
01:20:45.166 --> 01:20:47.669
Sounds like someone stepped in
and did your job for you. huh?

952
01:20:47.752 --> 01:20:48.836
Why do you sound out of breath. Tony?

953
01:20:48.920 --> 01:20:50.129
I'm not. I was just jogging in the canyon.

954
01:20:50.213 --> 01:20:52.006
- I thought you were driving.
- Right. I was driving

955
01:20:52.090 --> 01:20:53.883
to the canyon. where I'm going to jog.

956
01:20:53.967 --> 01:20:56.302
You sure you don't have any tech
in that area I should know about?

957
01:20:56.386 --> 01:20:57.887
- Nope!
- Bogey spotted!

958
01:20:57.971 --> 01:21:00.723
- Whiplash. come in hot.
- Okay. good. 'cause I'm staring at one

959
01:21:00.807 --> 01:21:04.185
right now. and it's about to be blown
to kingdom come.

960
01:21:04.894 --> 01:21:06.646
That's my exit.

961
01:21:11.359 --> 01:21:14.821
Ballroom. this is Whiplash One.
I've got the bogey in my sights.

962
01:21:14.988 --> 01:21:16.447
Whiplash One. what is it?

963
01:21:16.531 --> 01:21:17.865
I've got no idea.

964
01:21:17.949 --> 01:21:20.285
- You have radio contact?
- Non responsive. sir.

965
01:21:20.368 --> 01:21:21.452
Then you are clear to engage.

966
01:21:23.496 --> 01:21:24.497
Hit it.

967
01:21:29.335 --> 01:21:32.338
That bogey just went supersonic.
I got a lock!

968
01:21:36.342 --> 01:21:38.344
- Inbound missile.
- Flares!

969
01:21:41.347 --> 01:21:43.975
Wait a second. Bogey deployed flares!

970
01:21:58.239 --> 01:21:59.490
Deploy flaps!

971
01:22:00.700 --> 01:22:01.909
Holy!

972
01:22:01.993 --> 01:22:03.578
That thing just jumped off the radar. sir.

973
01:22:03.661 --> 01:22:05.204
The sat visual has been lost.

974
01:22:05.288 --> 01:22:06.956
No way that's a UAV.

975
01:22:07.040 --> 01:22:08.207
What is it?

976
01:22:08.291 --> 01:22:09.834
I can't see anything.

977
01:22:09.917 --> 01:22:12.378
Whatever it was. it just bought the farm.

978
01:22:12.879 --> 01:22:15.506
I think bogey's been handled. sir.

979
01:22:24.891 --> 01:22:26.559
- Hello?
- Hi. Rhodey. it's me.

980
01:22:26.643 --> 01:22:28.311
- It's who?
- I'm sorry. it is me.

981
01:22:28.394 --> 01:22:29.687
You asked.
What you were asking about is me.

982
01:22:29.771 --> 01:22:31.272
No. see. this isn't a game.

983
01:22:31.356 --> 01:22:34.651
You do not send civilian equipment
into my active war zone.

984
01:22:34.734 --> 01:22:36.653
- You understand that?
- This is not a piece of equipment.

985
01:22:36.736 --> 01:22:39.572
I'm in it. It's a suit. It's me!

986
01:22:39.656 --> 01:22:42.075
Rhodey. you got anything for me?

987
01:22:43.242 --> 01:22:46.621
- Mark your position and return to base.
- Roger that. Ballroom.

988
01:22:48.831 --> 01:22:49.999
On your belly!

989
01:22:50.083 --> 01:22:51.959
It looks like a man!

990
01:22:52.168 --> 01:22:54.837
Shake him off! Roll! Roll!

991
01:23:02.887 --> 01:23:04.013
I'm hit! I'm hit!

992
01:23:04.097 --> 01:23:06.432
It's confirmed. He has been hit.

993
01:23:10.561 --> 01:23:12.563
Punch out! Punch out!

994
01:23:18.945 --> 01:23:20.697
Whiplash One down.

995
01:23:20.780 --> 01:23:22.365
Whiplash Two. do you see a chute?

996
01:23:22.448 --> 01:23:24.701
Negative! No chute. no chute!

997
01:23:30.206 --> 01:23:31.624
My chute's jammed!

998
01:23:37.630 --> 01:23:39.966
Sir. I've got a visual on the bogey.

999
01:23:40.049 --> 01:23:42.677
Whiplash Two. reengage.
If you get a clear shot. you take it.

1000
01:23:45.221 --> 01:23:47.056
Major. we don't even know
what we're shooting at.

1001
01:23:47.140 --> 01:23:49.225
- Call off the Raptors.
- That thing just took out an F-22

1002
01:23:49.308 --> 01:23:50.643
inside a legal no fly zone!

1003
01:23:50.727 --> 01:23:53.062
Whiplash Two.
if you have a clear shot. take it!

1004
01:23:53.146 --> 01:23:55.523
You've been reengaged.
Execute evasive maneuver.

1005
01:23:55.606 --> 01:23:56.983
Keep going!

1006
01:24:04.574 --> 01:24:06.617
Good chute! Good chute!

1007
01:24:14.208 --> 01:24:17.086
- Tony. you still there?
- Hey. thanks.

1008
01:24:17.170 --> 01:24:19.756
Oh. my God. you crazy son of a bitch.

1009
01:24:20.548 --> 01:24:22.008
You owe me a plane.
You know that. right?

1010
01:24:23.760 --> 01:24:26.220
Yeah. well. technically. he hit me.

1011
01:24:26.304 --> 01:24:27.889
Now are you going to come by
and see what I'm working on?

1012
01:24:27.972 --> 01:24:30.850
No. no. no. no. no. no.
the less I know. the better.

1013
01:24:31.017 --> 01:24:32.560
Now. what am I supposed
to tell the press?

1014
01:24:32.643 --> 01:24:35.146
Training exercise.
Isn't that the usual BS?

1015
01:24:35.229 --> 01:24:36.981
It's not that simple.

1016
01:24:37.857 --> 01:24:39.609
An unfortunate training exercise

1017
01:24:39.692 --> 01:24:42.570
involving an F-22 Raptor
occurred yesterday.

1018
01:24:43.321 --> 01:24:46.699
I am pleased to report
that the pilot was not injured.

1019
01:24:46.783 --> 01:24:50.703
As for the unexpected turn of events
on the ground in Gulmira.

1020
01:24:50.787 --> 01:24:54.290
it is still unclear
who or what intervened.

1021
01:24:54.373 --> 01:24:58.544
but I can assure you that the United
States government was not involved.

1022
01:25:00.546 --> 01:25:01.672
Hey!

1023
01:25:03.549 --> 01:25:05.426
It is a tight fit. sir.

1024
01:25:06.427 --> 01:25:09.305
Sir. the more you struggle.
the more this is going to hurt.

1025
01:25:09.388 --> 01:25:11.349
Be gentle. This is my first time.

1026
01:25:12.225 --> 01:25:15.061
I designed this to come off. so... Hey.

1027
01:25:16.312 --> 01:25:20.066
- I really should be able to...
- Please. try not to move. sir.

1028
01:25:21.609 --> 01:25:23.903
What's going on here?

1029
01:25:28.449 --> 01:25:32.537
Let's face it. This is not the worst
thing you've caught me doing.

1030
01:25:33.079 --> 01:25:34.956
Are those bullet holes?

1031
01:26:02.441 --> 01:26:03.651
Welcome.

1032
01:26:07.029 --> 01:26:09.115
Compliments of Tony Stark.

1033
01:26:10.074 --> 01:26:13.703
If you'd killed him when you were
supposed to. you'd still have a face.

1034
01:26:13.786 --> 01:26:15.872
You paid us trinkets to kill a prince.

1035
01:26:15.955 --> 01:26:17.748
Show me the weapon.

1036
01:26:18.958 --> 01:26:22.461
Come. Leave your guards outside.

1037
01:26:39.228 --> 01:26:41.772
His escape bore unexpected fruit.

1038
01:26:44.442 --> 01:26:46.402
So this is how he did it.

1039
01:26:46.736 --> 01:26:49.238
This is only a first. crude effort.

1040
01:26:49.447 --> 01:26:51.741
Stark has perfected his design.

1041
01:26:52.158 --> 01:26:54.660
He has made a masterpiece of death.

1042
01:26:55.328 --> 01:26:58.497
A man with a dozen of these
can rule all of Asia.

1043
01:27:00.124 --> 01:27:02.460
And you dream of Stark's throne.

1044
01:27:04.253 --> 01:27:06.505
We have a common enemy.

1045
01:27:10.801 --> 01:27:12.762
If we are still in business.

1046
01:27:15.306 --> 01:27:17.516
I will give you these designs

1047
01:27:19.018 --> 01:27:20.019
as a gift.

1048
01:27:21.687 --> 01:27:23.064
And in turn.

1049
01:27:24.732 --> 01:27:29.862
I hope you'll repay me with
a gift of iron soldiers.

1050
01:27:40.831 --> 01:27:43.793
This is the only gift you shall receive.

1051
01:27:46.796 --> 01:27:48.172
Technology.

1052
01:27:50.049 --> 01:27:53.552
It's always been your Achilles' heel
in this part of the world.

1053
01:27:54.762 --> 01:27:57.932
Don't worry. It'll only
last for 15 minutes.

1054
01:27:59.141 --> 01:28:01.560
That's the least of your problems.

1055
01:28:06.816 --> 01:28:09.443
Crate up the armor and the rest of it.

1056
01:28:11.070 --> 01:28:13.114
All right. let's finish up here.

1057
01:28:17.076 --> 01:28:19.996
Set up Sector 16
underneath the arc reactor.

1058
01:28:20.079 --> 01:28:23.624
and I'm going to want this data masked.
Recruit our top engineers.

1059
01:28:23.708 --> 01:28:25.584
I want a prototype right away.

1060
01:28:33.759 --> 01:28:36.929
Hey. You busy?
You mind if I send you on an errand?

1061
01:28:37.013 --> 01:28:39.265
I need you to go to my office.

1062
01:28:39.765 --> 01:28:42.184
You're going to hack into the mainframe
and you're going to retrieve all

1063
01:28:42.268 --> 01:28:44.854
the recent shipping manifests.
This is a lock chip.

1064
01:28:44.937 --> 01:28:46.522
This'll get you in.

1065
01:28:46.605 --> 01:28:48.190
It's probably under Executive Files.

1066
01:28:48.274 --> 01:28:50.693
If not. they put it on a ghost drive.
in which case you need

1067
01:28:50.776 --> 01:28:53.446
to look for the lowest numeric heading.

1068
01:28:53.738 --> 01:28:56.198
And what do you plan to do with
this information if I bring it back here?

1069
01:28:56.282 --> 01:28:57.366
Same drill.

1070
01:28:57.450 --> 01:28:59.452
They've been dealing under the table.
and I'm going to stop them.

1071
01:28:59.535 --> 01:29:02.621
I'm going to find my weapons
and destroy them.

1072
01:29:03.581 --> 01:29:04.623
Tony.

1073
01:29:06.959 --> 01:29:08.836
you know that
I would help you with anything.

1074
01:29:08.919 --> 01:29:12.882
but I cannot help you if
you're going to start all of this again.

1075
01:29:12.965 --> 01:29:16.594
There is nothing except this.
There's no art opening.

1076
01:29:16.844 --> 01:29:20.056
There is no benefit.
There is nothing to sign.

1077
01:29:21.182 --> 01:29:24.268
There is the next mission
and nothing else.

1078
01:29:25.478 --> 01:29:26.812
Is that so?

1079
01:29:28.981 --> 01:29:30.483
Well. then. I quit.

1080
01:29:33.569 --> 01:29:35.196
You stood by my side all these years

1081
01:29:35.279 --> 01:29:38.115
while I reaped
the benefits of destruction.

1082
01:29:38.407 --> 01:29:40.242
And now that I'm trying
to protect the people

1083
01:29:40.326 --> 01:29:42.161
that I put in harm's way.
you're going to walk out?

1084
01:29:42.244 --> 01:29:46.707
You're going to kill yourself. Tony.
I'm not going to be a part of it.

1085
01:29:46.791 --> 01:29:48.793
I shouldn't be alive.

1086
01:29:50.086 --> 01:29:52.213
unless it was for a reason.

1087
01:29:53.047 --> 01:29:54.924
I'm not crazy. Pepper.

1088
01:29:55.424 --> 01:29:58.594
I just finally know what I have to do.

1089
01:30:02.932 --> 01:30:05.726
And I know in my heart that it's right.

1090
01:30:21.450 --> 01:30:23.869
You're all I have. too. you know.

1091
01:31:33.439 --> 01:31:38.277
Sector 16?
What are you up to. Obadiah?

1092
01:31:51.165 --> 01:31:55.502
You did not tell us that the target you
paid us to kill was the great Tony Stark.

1093
01:31:55.586 --> 01:31:57.129
- As you can see. Obadiah Stane...
- Oh. my God.

1094
01:31:57.213 --> 01:31:59.924
...Your deception and lies
will cost you dearly.

1095
01:32:00.007 --> 01:32:02.718
The price to kill Tony Stark
has just gone up.

1096
01:32:06.722 --> 01:32:11.143
So. what are we going to do about this?

1097
01:32:23.113 --> 01:32:26.408
I know what you're going through.
Pepper.

1098
01:32:34.124 --> 01:32:37.836
Tony. He always gets the good stuff.
doesn't he?

1099
01:32:59.441 --> 01:33:03.821
I was so happy when he came home.

1100
01:33:03.904 --> 01:33:06.699
It was like we got him back
from the dead.

1101
01:33:09.743 --> 01:33:11.704
Now I realize.

1102
01:33:14.039 --> 01:33:17.293
well. Tony never really did
come home. did he?

1103
01:33:19.044 --> 01:33:21.714
He left a part of himself in that cave.

1104
01:33:24.508 --> 01:33:26.093
Breaks my heart.

1105
01:33:28.387 --> 01:33:32.391
Well. he's a complicated person.

1106
01:33:35.060 --> 01:33:38.480
He's been through a lot.
I think he'll be all right.

1107
01:33:44.778 --> 01:33:47.573
You are a very rare woman.

1108
01:33:50.075 --> 01:33:52.244
Tony doesn't know how lucky he is.

1109
01:33:54.955 --> 01:33:56.957
Thank you. Thanks.

1110
01:33:58.959 --> 01:34:01.003
I'd better get back there.

1111
01:34:06.467 --> 01:34:08.510
Is that today's paper?

1112
01:34:10.137 --> 01:34:11.221
Yes.

1113
01:34:11.972 --> 01:34:13.390
Do you mind?

1114
01:34:13.974 --> 01:34:15.809
- Not at all.
- Puzzle.

1115
01:34:15.893 --> 01:34:17.227
Of course.

1116
01:34:20.689 --> 01:34:22.024
Take care.

1117
01:34:46.173 --> 01:34:49.051
Ms. Potts? We had an appointment.
Did you forget about our appointment?

1118
01:34:49.134 --> 01:34:50.677
Nope. right now. Come with me.

1119
01:34:50.761 --> 01:34:51.887
- Right now?
- We're going to have it right now.

1120
01:34:51.970 --> 01:34:53.764
- Yeah. walk with me.
- Okay.

1121
01:34:54.932 --> 01:34:57.059
I'm going to give you the meeting
of your life. Your office.

1122
01:34:58.644 --> 01:35:01.480
Yeah. we've been working
our best to do it.

1123
01:35:01.855 --> 01:35:05.401
Absolutely. we're...
I'm going to have to call you back.

1124
01:35:05.609 --> 01:35:08.278
Mr. Stane? Sir. we've explored

1125
01:35:08.362 --> 01:35:10.614
what you've asked us. and it seems
as though there's a little hiccup.

1126
01:35:10.697 --> 01:35:12.408
- Actually...
- A hiccup?

1127
01:35:12.491 --> 01:35:16.328
Yes. to power the suit. sir.
the technology actually doesn't exist.

1128
01:35:16.495 --> 01:35:19.665
- So it's...
- Wait. wait. wait. The technology?

1129
01:35:19.748 --> 01:35:25.754
William. here is the technology.
I've asked you to simply make it smaller.

1130
01:35:25.838 --> 01:35:29.800
Okay. sir. and that's what we're trying
to do. but honestly. it's impossible.

1131
01:35:29.883 --> 01:35:36.515
Tony Stark was able to build this
in a cave! With a box of scraps!

1132
01:35:38.684 --> 01:35:41.770
Well. I'm sorry. I'm not Tony Stark.

1133
01:35:57.870 --> 01:35:58.871
Tony?

1134
01:36:01.623 --> 01:36:04.918
Tony. are you there? Hello?

1135
01:36:06.503 --> 01:36:07.713
Breathe.

1136
01:36:08.881 --> 01:36:11.633
Easy. easy.

1137
01:36:13.719 --> 01:36:16.013
You remember this one. right?

1138
01:36:17.723 --> 01:36:20.017
It's a shame the government
didn't approve it.

1139
01:36:20.100 --> 01:36:24.229
There's so many applications
for causing short-term paralysis.

1140
01:36:26.565 --> 01:36:27.858
Tony.

1141
01:36:30.152 --> 01:36:34.531
When I ordered the hit on you.

1142
01:36:37.117 --> 01:36:39.620
I worried that I was

1143
01:36:42.664 --> 01:36:44.708
killing the golden goose.

1144
01:36:46.043 --> 01:36:49.796
But. you see. it was just

1145
01:36:51.131 --> 01:36:53.425
fate that you survived that.

1146
01:36:58.472 --> 01:37:02.351
You had one last golden egg to give.

1147
01:37:06.522 --> 01:37:11.818
Do you really think that just because
you have an idea. it belongs to you?

1148
01:37:15.739 --> 01:37:20.869
Your father. he helped give us
the atomic bomb.

1149
01:37:20.953 --> 01:37:25.207
Now. what kind of world would it be
today if he was as selfish as you?

1150
01:37:35.175 --> 01:37:36.843
Oh. it's beautiful.

1151
01:37:39.471 --> 01:37:44.309
Tony. this is your Ninth Symphony.

1152
01:37:46.603 --> 01:37:49.064
What a masterpiece. Look at that.

1153
01:37:50.440 --> 01:37:52.192
This is your legacy.

1154
01:37:54.736 --> 01:37:59.950
A new generation of weapons
with this at its heart.

1155
01:38:03.161 --> 01:38:06.873
Weapons that will help steer the world
back on course.

1156
01:38:06.957 --> 01:38:09.209
put the balance of power in our hands.

1157
01:38:10.794 --> 01:38:12.421
The right hands.

1158
01:38:15.549 --> 01:38:20.095
I wish you could see my prototype.

1159
01:38:21.513 --> 01:38:23.015
It's not as...

1160
01:38:24.349 --> 01:38:27.352
Well. not as conservative as yours.

1161
01:38:29.354 --> 01:38:32.190
Too bad you had to involve Pepper
in this.

1162
01:38:32.649 --> 01:38:35.235
I would have preferred that she lived.

1163
01:38:48.248 --> 01:38:50.542
What do you mean.
he paid to have Tony killed?

1164
01:38:50.626 --> 01:38:53.253
Pepper. slow down.
Why would Obadiah...

1165
01:38:54.504 --> 01:38:55.797
Okay. where's Tony now?

1166
01:38:55.881 --> 01:38:57.591
I don't know.
He's not answering his phone.

1167
01:38:57.674 --> 01:38:59.801
Please go over there
and make sure everything's okay.

1168
01:38:59.885 --> 01:39:02.512
Thank you. Rhodey. I know a shortcut.

1169
01:40:08.829 --> 01:40:10.122
Good boy.

1170
01:40:49.953 --> 01:40:51.037
Tony?

1171
01:40:53.665 --> 01:40:54.791
Tony?

1172
01:40:56.543 --> 01:40:57.669
Tony?

1173
01:40:59.796 --> 01:41:00.922
Tony?

1174
01:41:03.592 --> 01:41:04.676
Tony!

1175
01:41:06.887 --> 01:41:09.181
Tony! You okay?

1176
01:41:09.514 --> 01:41:13.143
- Where's Pepper?
- She's fine. She's with five agents.

1177
01:41:13.226 --> 01:41:15.562
They're about to arrest Obadiah.

1178
01:41:15.687 --> 01:41:17.814
That's not going to be enough.

1179
01:41:41.630 --> 01:41:47.636
Section 16. Section 16. There it is.

1180
01:41:56.645 --> 01:41:59.314
My key's not working.
It's not opening the door.

1181
01:41:59.397 --> 01:42:01.566
Oh. wow! What's that?
It's. like. a little device?

1182
01:42:01.650 --> 01:42:03.068
It's. like. a thing that's going
to pick the lock?

1183
01:42:03.151 --> 01:42:05.904
You might want to take
a few steps back.

1184
01:42:24.464 --> 01:42:27.008
That's the coolest thing I've ever seen.

1185
01:42:27.092 --> 01:42:29.886
Not bad. huh? Let's do it.

1186
01:42:36.560 --> 01:42:38.937
You need me to do anything else?

1187
01:42:39.521 --> 01:42:41.314
Keep the skies clear.

1188
01:42:46.444 --> 01:42:47.737
Damn!

1189
01:42:55.787 --> 01:42:57.455
Next time. baby.

1190
01:43:27.569 --> 01:43:30.947
Looks like you were right.
He was building a suit.

1191
01:43:31.531 --> 01:43:33.533
I thought it'd be bigger.

1192
01:44:18.370 --> 01:44:19.537
Take him out!

1193
01:44:30.256 --> 01:44:32.258
How do you think the Mark I
chest piece is going to hold up?

1194
01:44:32.342 --> 01:44:34.636
The suit's at 48% power and falling. sir.

1195
01:44:34.719 --> 01:44:37.430
That chest piece
was never designed for sustained flight.

1196
01:44:37.514 --> 01:44:39.057
Keep me posted.

1197
01:44:40.809 --> 01:44:41.810
Pepper!

1198
01:44:41.893 --> 01:44:44.896
- Tony! Tony. are you okay?
- I'm fine. How are...

1199
01:44:44.980 --> 01:44:46.898
- Obadiah. he's gone insane!
- I know.

1200
01:44:46.982 --> 01:44:48.775
- Listen. you'd better get out of there.
- He built a suit.

1201
01:44:48.858 --> 01:44:50.318
Get out of there right now!

1202
01:45:02.163 --> 01:45:04.499
Where do you think you're going?

1203
01:45:10.005 --> 01:45:13.008
Your services are no longer required.

1204
01:45:13.216 --> 01:45:14.676
Stane!

1205
01:45:39.868 --> 01:45:41.536
I love this suit!

1206
01:45:41.619 --> 01:45:44.873
- Put them down!
- Collateral damage. Tony.

1207
01:45:46.416 --> 01:45:48.460
Divert power to chest RT.

1208
01:45:57.177 --> 01:45:59.304
Power reduced to 19%.

1209
01:46:07.145 --> 01:46:08.271
Lady!

1210
01:46:10.148 --> 01:46:12.192
No. no. no. no. no. no!

1211
01:46:34.255 --> 01:46:37.217
For 30 years. I've been holding you up!

1212
01:46:41.679 --> 01:46:44.140
I built this company from nothing!

1213
01:46:46.392 --> 01:46:48.978
Nothing is going to stand in my way.

1214
01:46:55.235 --> 01:46:57.779
Least of all you!

1215
01:47:07.205 --> 01:47:10.458
Impressive!
You've upgraded your armor!

1216
01:47:11.042 --> 01:47:13.753
I've made some upgrades of my own!

1217
01:47:22.095 --> 01:47:24.055
Sir. it appears that his suit can fly.

1218
01:47:24.139 --> 01:47:25.807
Duly noted.
Take me to maximum altitude.

1219
01:47:25.890 --> 01:47:28.184
With only 15% power.
the odds of reaching that...

1220
01:47:28.268 --> 01:47:30.436
I know the math! Do it!

1221
01:47:38.736 --> 01:47:41.030
Sir. you're not going to believe this.
That thing is back.

1222
01:47:41.114 --> 01:47:43.741
Get me Major Allen. Scramble the jets!

1223
01:47:46.452 --> 01:47:49.455
Not necessary. people.
Just a training exercise.

1224
01:47:49.539 --> 01:47:50.790
Yes. sir.

1225
01:47:58.756 --> 01:48:00.675
- Thirteen percent power. sir.
- Climb!

1226
01:48:04.679 --> 01:48:06.723
- Eleven percent.
- Keep going!

1227
01:48:13.438 --> 01:48:15.565
- Seven percent power.
- Just leave it on the screen!

1228
01:48:15.648 --> 01:48:17.275
Stop telling me!

1229
01:48:26.951 --> 01:48:31.539
You had a great idea. Tony. but my
suit is more advanced in every way!

1230
01:48:32.123 --> 01:48:34.167
How'd you solve the icing problem?

1231
01:48:34.250 --> 01:48:35.752
Icing problem?

1232
01:48:37.962 --> 01:48:40.298
Might want to look into it.

1233
01:48:51.976 --> 01:48:53.311
Two percent.

1234
01:48:55.438 --> 01:48:58.316
We are now running
on emergency backup power.

1235
01:49:09.953 --> 01:49:13.414
- Potts!
- Tony! Oh. my God. are you okay?

1236
01:49:13.498 --> 01:49:17.627
I'm almost out of power. I've got to get
out of this thing. I'll be right there.

1237
01:49:17.710 --> 01:49:19.128
Nice try!

1238
01:49:31.683 --> 01:49:35.812
- Weapons status?
- Repulsors offline. Missiles offline.

1239
01:49:40.066 --> 01:49:41.651
Flares!

1240
01:49:50.159 --> 01:49:52.203
Very clever. Tony.

1241
01:49:57.542 --> 01:50:00.003
- Potts?
- Tony!

1242
01:50:00.086 --> 01:50:01.087
This isn't working.

1243
01:50:01.170 --> 01:50:03.464
We're going to have to overload
the reactor and blast the roof.

1244
01:50:03.548 --> 01:50:06.426
- Well. how are you going to do that?
- You're going to do it.

1245
01:50:06.509 --> 01:50:08.970
Go to the central console.
open up all the circuits.

1246
01:50:09.053 --> 01:50:10.471
When I get clear of the roof.
I'll let you know.

1247
01:50:10.555 --> 01:50:13.141
You're going to hit
the master bypass button.

1248
01:50:13.224 --> 01:50:14.600
It's going to fry everything up here.

1249
01:50:16.769 --> 01:50:19.063
Okay. I'm going in now.

1250
01:50:19.147 --> 01:50:22.400
Make sure you wait till I clear the roof.
I'll buy you some time.

1251
01:50:31.909 --> 01:50:33.745
This looks important!

1252
01:50:54.599 --> 01:50:57.393
I never had a taste for this sort of thing.

1253
01:50:57.477 --> 01:51:01.606
but I must admit.
I'm deeply enjoying the suit!

1254
01:51:09.864 --> 01:51:12.367
You finally outdid yourself. Tony!

1255
01:51:14.744 --> 01:51:16.871
You'd have made your father proud!

1256
01:51:21.834 --> 01:51:24.337
It's ready. Tony! Get off the roof!

1257
01:51:43.856 --> 01:51:45.191
Tony!

1258
01:51:46.401 --> 01:51:48.027
How ironic. Tony!

1259
01:51:49.821 --> 01:51:54.742
Trying to rid the world of weapons.
you gave it its best one ever!

1260
01:51:54.992 --> 01:52:00.873
- Pepper!
- And now I'm going to kill you with it!

1261
01:52:03.918 --> 01:52:07.755
- You ripped out my targeting system!
- Time to hit the button!

1262
01:52:07.839 --> 01:52:11.843
- You told me not to!
- Hold still. you little prick!

1263
01:52:13.886 --> 01:52:16.472
- Just do it!
- You'll die!

1264
01:52:19.559 --> 01:52:21.060
Push it!

1265
01:53:18.618 --> 01:53:20.411
Tony!

1266
01:53:28.836 --> 01:53:30.963
You've all received the official
statement of what occurred

1267
01:53:31.047 --> 01:53:33.341
at Stark Industries last night.

1268
01:53:33.674 --> 01:53:38.221
There have been unconfirmed reports
that a robotic prototype malfunctioned

1269
01:53:38.304 --> 01:53:40.932
and caused damage to the arc reactor.

1270
01:53:41.641 --> 01:53:43.893
Fortunately. a member
of Tony Stark's personal security staff...

1271
01:53:43.976 --> 01:53:45.895
"Iron Man." That's kind of catchy.
It's got a nice ring to it.

1272
01:53:45.978 --> 01:53:49.649
I mean. it's not technically accurate.
The suit's a gold-titanium alloy.

1273
01:53:49.732 --> 01:53:52.360
but it's kind of evocative.
the imagery. anyway.

1274
01:53:52.443 --> 01:53:54.111
Here's your alibi.

1275
01:53:54.946 --> 01:53:56.030
Okay.

1276
01:53:56.113 --> 01:53:58.282
- You were on your yacht.
- Yeah.

1277
01:53:58.366 --> 01:54:00.493
We have port papers that put you
in Avalon all night.

1278
01:54:00.576 --> 01:54:02.286
and sworn statements
from 50 of your guests.

1279
01:54:02.370 --> 01:54:05.498
See. I was thinking maybe we should
say it was just Pepper and me

1280
01:54:05.581 --> 01:54:07.375
alone on the island.

1281
01:54:08.668 --> 01:54:09.961
- That's what happened.
- All right.

1282
01:54:10.044 --> 01:54:12.171
Just read it. word for word.

1283
01:54:14.090 --> 01:54:16.092
There's nothing about Stane here.

1284
01:54:16.175 --> 01:54:18.970
That's being handled. He's on vacation.

1285
01:54:19.845 --> 01:54:22.306
Small aircraft have
such a poor safety record.

1286
01:54:22.390 --> 01:54:24.892
But what about the whole cover story
that it's a bodyguard?

1287
01:54:24.976 --> 01:54:27.895
He's my... I mean. is that...
That's kind of flimsy. don't you think?

1288
01:54:27.979 --> 01:54:30.273
This isn't my first rodeo. Mr. Stark.

1289
01:54:30.356 --> 01:54:34.360
Just stick to the official statement.
and soon. this will all be behind you.

1290
01:54:34.443 --> 01:54:36.696
You've got 90 seconds.

1291
01:54:39.574 --> 01:54:41.242
Agent Coulson?

1292
01:54:41.909 --> 01:54:46.414
I just wanted to say thank you very much
for all of your help.

1293
01:54:46.497 --> 01:54:49.417
That's what we do.
You'll be hearing from us.

1294
01:54:49.667 --> 01:54:53.045
- From the Strategic Homeland...
- Just call us S.H.I.E.L.D.

1295
01:54:53.379 --> 01:54:54.547
Right.

1296
01:54:55.506 --> 01:54:59.427
- Let's get this show on the road.
- You know. it's actually not that bad.

1297
01:54:59.510 --> 01:55:01.804
Even I don't think I'm Iron Man.

1298
01:55:01.887 --> 01:55:03.431
- You're not Iron Man.
- Am so.

1299
01:55:03.514 --> 01:55:05.975
- You're not.
- All right. suit yourself.

1300
01:55:06.058 --> 01:55:10.062
You know. if I were Iron Man. I'd have
this girlfriend who knew my true identity.

1301
01:55:10.146 --> 01:55:12.690
She'd be a wreck. 'cause she'd always
be worrying that I was going to die.

1302
01:55:12.773 --> 01:55:15.151
yet so proud of the man I'd become.

1303
01:55:15.234 --> 01:55:18.988
She'd be wildly conflicted.
which would only make her more

1304
01:55:20.698 --> 01:55:21.741
crazy about me.

1305
01:55:21.824 --> 01:55:23.492
Tell me you never think about that night.

1306
01:55:23.576 --> 01:55:25.453
- What night?
- You know.

1307
01:55:28.372 --> 01:55:34.170
Are you talking about the night that
we danced and went up on the roof.

1308
01:55:35.796 --> 01:55:41.385
and then you went downstairs
to get me a drink.

1309
01:55:41.469 --> 01:55:44.722
and you left me there. by myself?

1310
01:55:45.931 --> 01:55:48.476
Is that the night you're talking about?

1311
01:55:50.645 --> 01:55:51.729
Thought so.

1312
01:55:54.440 --> 01:55:58.194
- Will that be all. Mr. Stark?
- Yes. that will be all. Miss Potts.

1313
01:55:58.277 --> 01:56:01.822
And now. Mr. Stark has
prepared a statement.

1314
01:56:01.906 --> 01:56:04.950
He will not be taking any questions.
Thank you.

1315
01:56:09.121 --> 01:56:14.251
Been a while since I was in front of you.
I figure I'll stick to the cards this time.

1316
01:56:16.212 --> 01:56:19.256
There's been speculation that I was
involved in the events that occurred

1317
01:56:19.340 --> 01:56:20.633
on the freeway and the rooftop...

1318
01:56:20.716 --> 01:56:23.511
I'm sorry. Mr. Stark. but do you
honestly expect us to believe that

1319
01:56:23.594 --> 01:56:27.348
that was a bodyguard
in a suit that conveniently appeared.

1320
01:56:27.431 --> 01:56:30.518
- despite the fact that you...
- I know that it's confusing.

1321
01:56:30.601 --> 01:56:34.230
It is one thing to question the official
story. and another thing entirely

1322
01:56:34.313 --> 01:56:37.566
to make wild accusations.
or insinuate that I'm a superhero.

1323
01:56:37.650 --> 01:56:39.276
I never said you were a superhero.

1324
01:56:39.360 --> 01:56:44.699
Didn't? Well. good. because that would
be outlandish and fantastic.

1325
01:56:46.701 --> 01:56:49.954
I'm just not the hero type. Clearly.

1326
01:56:50.496 --> 01:56:53.457
With this laundry list
of character defects.

1327
01:56:53.541 --> 01:56:55.000
all the mistakes I've made.

1328
01:56:55.084 --> 01:56:58.421
- largely public.
- Just stick to the cards. man.

1329
01:56:58.504 --> 01:57:00.172
Yeah. okay. Yeah.

1330
01:57:02.299 --> 01:57:03.801
The truth is

1331
01:57:09.974 --> 01:57:11.475
I am Iron Man.

1332
02:05:14.708 --> 02:05:15.959
Jarvis!

1333
02:05:16.043 --> 02:05:17.794
Welcome home. sir.

1334
02:05:21.215 --> 02:05:26.720
"I am Iron Man." You think you're
the only superhero in the world?

1335
02:05:27.054 --> 02:05:30.307
Mr. Stark. you've become part
of a bigger universe.

1336
02:05:30.390 --> 02:05:32.184
You just don't know it yet.

1337
02:05:32.684 --> 02:05:34.478
Who the hell are you?

1338
02:05:34.686 --> 02:05:37.397
Nick Fury. Director of S.H.I.E.L.D.

1339
02:05:39.483 --> 02:05:42.486
I'm here to talk to you
about the Avenger initiative.
